ked Hunter during the Dark Eras, so I only feeds upon what I read in the threads and some spoilers, hence why I'm not sure how much I could contribute to the discussion- but I have posted my thoughts about Changelings in the Neolithic in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/857526-neolithic-era-for-everyone?p=858367#post858367\">here</a>, basing it around the Curse of Sleep written by Arc. I'm also on the &quot;not only Strix and Revenants&quot; camp, and I really do enjoy Clair's thoughts about the subject. Anyway, from what I've gathered, I think that exploring Sin Eaters during that Era, considering that they are described making pacts with chthonic beings which were never born or something like that- after all, if geists are ghosts who rose in Rank to become archetypes of their own death, and we can assume that until the recent change in the state of the Underworld geists wouldn't be able to go out- than what the hell the Bound of that Era make Bargains with? A lot of potential for pre-humanity ghosts and other such weirdness, I think.<br /> <br /> As for the Purified, I would have preferred to see them as a full, major template than a microtemplate- they are too inhuman compared to the ones presented in Hurt Locker, and they do have their own set of powers and signature Supernatural Tolerance trait and use supernatural energy to power themselves (as Essence). They may be few in numbers, sure, but they are still more powerful than the average &quot;minor template&quot;, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T14:45:47-07:00","id":869676,"title":"","content":"I think Dave said elsewhere that Sin-Eaters were bound to Cthonians rather than Geists in the Neolithic era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T18:14:27-07:00","id":869787,"title":"","content":"I definitely like the idea of Kindred Bloodlines emerging from the groups of Revenants and Strix, but I'm also of the opinion that most vampires out there are Revenants. Not too many Kindred out there to do the Embracing, and those that are seem likely to be spawning from the Synthesis Embodiment, and from Neglatu-like Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I really love the idea of Sin-Eaters in this era making the Bargain with Cthonians- they're probably even more alien than Geists and definitely more eldritch. I imagine the Stygian Key and the Pit Manifestation are a good deal more common. How do you think a Cthonian Bound differs from a Geist Bound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T18:26:58-07:00","id":869793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=869787#post869787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely like the idea of Kindred Bloodlines emerging from the groups of Revenants and Strix, but I'm also of the opinion that most vampires out there are Revenants. Not too many Kindred out there to do the Embracing, and those that are seem likely to be spawning from the Synthesis Embodiment, and from Neglatu-like Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I really love the idea of Sin-Eaters in this era making the Bargain with Cthonians- they're probably even more alien than Geists and definitely more eldritch. I imagine the Stygian Key and the Pit Manifestation are a good deal more common. How do you think a Cthonian Bound differs from a Geist Bound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chthonians entirely lack humanity, so I see Sin-Eaters of the time becoming more or less embodiments of death, given they're tied now to something that by their very definition never lived. They probably have similar thresholds, but the archetypes themselves are likely skewed to filter through the lens of something without any sort of human perspective sharing their mind. Very few Sin-Eaters care about gatekeeping for the sake of separating the realms and dont directly keep people out or ghosts in, but might have a focus on Gates and how they properly need to be placed within the world, for instance. Far more likely rely on ghost-eating and similar.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, I see Synergy being changed a lot. In fact, they might have something more in reverse; something akin to a lack of embodiment of the Chthonian's nature, retaining their more human perspective, and the lower it goes, the more they become a simple embodiment of some aspect of death and nothing more. I can also see them having Ceremonies or something else that reflect the Death influence Cthonians have, mirroring some awakened spells in a way similar to how proximi do, but always acting as a ritual. Summoners talks about how they might be something ELSE simply cut off from the supernal (like some say pangeans were), so it makes sense, I think.<br /> <br /> Overall, Sin-Eaters would just be... a lot scarier overall. Not someone you want hanging around, and not the cheery life celebrators you see today.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T23:26:14-07:00","id":869974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=869676#post869676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Dave said elsewhere that Sin-Eaters were bound to Cthonians rather than Geists in the Neolithic era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah - it says that <i>in the Dark Era</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-20T23:29:13-07:00","id":869975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=869974#post869974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah - it says that <i>in the Dark Era</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's possible not everyone remembered Chthonians are also called 'never-born'. But yeah I admittedly also forgot it blatantly said 'never-born', too XD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T00:23:25-07:00","id":869999,"title":"","content":"in that case, I think the following questions require some pondering-<br /> <br /> 1) how well are the Bound and the Chthonians are mixed together? Do they share body with the Sin Eater, like geists do? Or are they &quot;too big&quot;, leaving only a shard of themselves in the Bound's soul and mostly stay in the Underworld's cold water?<br /> <br /> 2) Why did they stopped making Bargains? Is it simply because the Ocean dropped so much, leaving them behind so far upon different levels of the Underworld away like gasping fish after the tide? After all, scientifically speaking, the effect of forces depends strongly on distance, and Death acts somewhat like gravity- but this is not science. What stops a modern Chthonian- or any other scary Underworld being- from making a Bargain? When did the geists learned how to offer Bargains on their own?<br /> <br /> 3) What the chthonians are exactly? Yeah, that question was left open even at Book of the Dead, but still i think it would be cool to see what the Bound of that age has to say about it.<br /> <br /> It would also be interesting to explore the beginning of the Bound society- I assume that many of them won't be qualified as &quot;Sin Eater&quot;- that is, working to deal with ghosts and help the dead to move on or things like that. The establishment of the first krewes, the creation of the first mythologies, perhaps the beginning of the Twilight Network- so much to explore, not to mention the great change that goes down in the Underworld. How long for it for the first Death Lord to rise and establish his own Dominion, Kereboi and everything?<br /> <br /> Also, while checking my homebrew signature, I've apparently wrote down a race of &quot;advanced cryptids&quot; called the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/439745-antagonists-the-grigori\">Grigori </a>which were created by the God Machine in the early times as a &quot;beta version&quot; for angels. Perhaps they could have some use in the Neolithic setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 04-21-2016, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T04:42:13-07:00","id":870088,"title":"","content":"I remember a writer, possibly during the KS, saying how he thought it'd be interesting if Sin-eaters didn't come around until medieval or renaissance times since that's kinda when the concept, or at least that phrase, came into being. That way it's not like every splat can just be traced back to the dawn of time but there's a dynamic history. So, for example, I don't mind if it's just Strix or revenants here.<br /> <br /> With that being said...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=868579#post868579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy: Obviously Azar and the Temakhs are present along the Nile. Not sure what to... do with them though. Obviously no Arisen yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the guy with a mummy as his avatar this is not okay and there must be a solution here. There was a time when the Shan'iatu traveled the world and took on many animalistic shapes, and later they taught their first acolytes sorcery. It's easy enough to handwave this as the Vinca encountering Shan'iatu, who are probably comparable to Pangaeans, and playing mortal sorcerers under their tutelage, and in these days said mortals could probably actually wield one or two tiers of an Utterance.<br /> <br /> But maybe this bit from Sothis Ascends can spur us a little further, talking about how the energies of a Sothic Turn might allow for time travel (coupled with the broken time shenanigans of this Neolithic Era):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sothis Ascends, pg. 107</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...explore a time completely unknown to even the Arisen. Modern humans may have existed over 100,000 years ago. What dark forces haunted those first people? Perhaps the Rite of Return is only the most recent event in a struggle that began millennia ago, and that may not end for another hundred millennia more.</div> </div> </div> </div>So aside from all the inspiration that oozes, we can have anachronistic future Arisen exploring this Era, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T07:13:34-07:00","id":870164,"title":"","content":"Nothing in what you said implies earlier Arisen to me. It implies the Temahks did/created other things entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-22-2016, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T07:37:28-07:00","id":870187,"title":"","content":"There is a way for Arisan to be in this setting. Time travel!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T08:54:58-07:00","id":870247,"title":"","content":"Irem may not rise for years to come with the Rite nearly a thousand years distant, but the Shan'iatu and Nameless Gods are timeless, and Sekhem has aleays been the stuff of the world. While this Era certainly lacks Arisen (and no, I don't like the idea of time travel back before the date of the Rite), it may be fun to instead explore the role of normal people or Wise that have been selected by the forces that will forge the Nameless Empire. <br /> <br /> Hell, you could do an awesome chronicle about the first Remet to take up weapons of stone and copper to tame the Black Land at the command of Nameless Gods, combating other tribes (and their supernatural patrons, for surely Irem did not rise unopposed) and rampaging demons from Duat as you raise the first pillars.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, you could simply play one of the Wise whose Awakening was stuffed with the symbols of Irem and the servants of Azar, or an early werewolf who serves a skeletal totemic hound who rules the dead as their king.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T10:19:45-07:00","id":870311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=869999#post869999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in that case, I think the following questions require some pondering-<br /> <br /> 1) how well are the Bound and the Chthonians are mixed together? Do they share body with the Sin Eater, like geists do? Or are they &amp;quot;too big&amp;quot;, leaving only a shard of themselves in the Bound's soul and mostly stay in the Underworld's cold water?<br /> <br /> 2) Why did they stopped making Bargains? Is it simply because the Ocean dropped so much, leaving them behind so far upon different levels of the Underworld away like gasping fish after the tide? After all, scientifically speaking, the effect of forces depends strongly on distance, and Death acts somewhat like gravity- but this is not science. What stops a modern Chthonian- or any other scary Underworld being- from making a Bargain? When did the geists learned how to offer Bargains on their own?<br /> <br /> 3) What the chthonians are exactly? Yeah, that question was left open even at Book of the Dead, but still i think it would be cool to see what the Bound of that age has to say about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... You know, between the Underworld's association with the sea in this Era and the theme of &quot;the world is a smaller place&quot; that seems a common thread in Sundered World Fannon, I have to wonder if there could be a connection between the Chthonians and the Makara. There are certainly some interesting parallels between Sin-Eaters and Begotten that could be fun to play with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T10:39:58-07:00","id":870336,"title":"","content":"wait- isn't there a theory that the Kereboi of the Ocean of Fragments is actually a Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:37:08-07:00","id":870388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=870336#post870336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait- isn't there a theory that the Kereboi of the Ocean of Fragments is actually a Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be. I'm not very well-versed in Beast yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T11:46:54-07:00","id":870404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=869999#post869999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">in that case, I think the following questions require some pondering-<br /> <br /> 1) how well are the Bound and the Chthonians are mixed together? Do they share body with the Sin Eater, like geists do? Or are they &quot;too big&quot;, leaving only a shard of themselves in the Bound's soul and mostly stay in the Underworld's cold water?<br /> <br /> 2) Why did they stopped making Bargains? Is it simply because the Ocean dropped so much, leaving them behind so far upon different levels of the Underworld away like gasping fish after the tide? After all, scientifically speaking, the effect of forces depends strongly on distance, and Death acts somewhat like gravity- but this is not science. What stops a modern Chthonian- or any other scary Underworld being- from making a Bargain? When did the geists learned how to offer Bargains on their own?<br /> <br /> 3) What the chthonians are exactly? Yeah, that question was left open even at Book of the Dead, but still i think it would be cool to see what the Bound of that age has to say about it.<br /> <br /> It would also be interesting to explore the beginning of the Bound society- I assume that many of them won't be qualified as &quot;Sin Eater&quot;- that is, working to deal with ghosts and help the dead to move on or things like that. The establishment of the first krewes, the creation of the first mythologies, perhaps the beginning of the Twilight Network- so much to explore, not to mention the great change that goes down in the Underworld. How long for it for the first Death Lord to rise and establish his own Dominion, Kereboi and everything?<br /> <br /> Also, while checking my homebrew signature, I've apparently wrote down a race of &quot;advanced cryptids&quot; called the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/439745-antagonists-the-grigori\">Grigori </a>which were created by the God Machine in the early times as a &quot;beta version&quot; for angels. Perhaps they could have some use in the Neolithic setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Chthonians can have the same ranks as spirits, based on what Summoners says, so I imagine the ones binding with Bound are those that can 'fit' in them, even if just barely.<br /> <br /> 2) It might be a statistical thing. That is, far, far fewer Chthonians actually WANT to make such a bargain, but in the Neolithic era that matches up with the low population just fine. However, nowadays Geists more or less flood that sort of dealmaking so it appears like they're the only ones that do it. Maybe there ARE Chthonian-Bound in modern times, they're just an incredible rarity? That could be its own interesting antagonist or just mysterious NPC in more modern times.<br /> <br /> 3) Summoners suggests they might be fragments of Stygia that have been cut off from it after Atlantis fell, and were left in the Underworld. However, if you want a less mage-centric cosmology, they might be similar to pangeans, having a connection to the supernal (only Death arcana in their case) but still being rooted in the Fallen. Unlike most of what's in the underworld, they're more archetypes of death that have formed in the depths of the Ocean, representing necromantic concepts more abstractly than pangeans who primarily take on the form of physical things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T12:35:47-07:00","id":870467,"title":"","content":"Oh, Sin-Eaters are going to be fun to look at in this era, <i>especially </i>since it means Cthonians will get a little more focus. Seeing as most ghosts that actually make it to the Ocean Beneath The World essentially get subsumed into it, unless they can manage to find a little island, I imagine these early Bound are trying to keep ghosts in the living world, both as allies and retainers <i>and </i>as a source of power.<br /> <br /> I imagine that much as the Wise have a hard time gathering Mana due to a lack of Hallows, Sin-Eaters have trouble finding Haunts. Ceremonies probably see a lot more use in this era, as the Bound is likely to become something of a natural cult leader and ritual master.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Anyways, here's a little something I whipped up for the Gudthabak, based on the 1E Rite of Renunciation but rewritten to fit the 2E Rite paradigm. This is meant to be an extremely difficult Rite to successfully perform, especially given that most places will be some level of Extreme Environment, and the effects of that will start to take a toll on the initiate.<br /> <br /> <b>Rite of Ascension (ooooo)</b><br /> <br /> Perhaps the most vital of all the Rites used by Bull's children, this is the ceremony devised to create their people, and ultimately, it is the Rite that is altered and transformed to save their people. It requires a subject who has been touched by the energy of a god, so either a descendent of the Gudthabak with a Tell, or one of the Wolf-Blooded. Performing this ritual requires either a fragment of one of Bull's omphalos stones, or a piece of Bull's shattered horns which gives all the rolls of this ritual the Rote action quality. To do so without either item is almost certain death. Should the Rite fail, and the subject <i>is not</i> touched by the power of a god, the subject dies in addition to any negative Conditions suffered by the Ritemaster. This Rite may only be performed on a given subject <i>once</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols: </b>Dominance, Resilience, Strength, Fertility, Transformation, Bulls<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite: </b>It is traditional for the Gudthabak to strip the subject of the Rite of all their possessions and place them amongst the herds of cattle. The Ritemaster is likely in their hybrid form, leading or driving the herd, while fellow Gudthabak take their great animal shape and mingle with the herd. The initiate must endure a gruelling trial, following the herds often into the wilds of Pangaea itself- never stopping, but persevering even in the face of brutal environmental conditions. Eventually, the Ritemaster and the other participating Gudthabak will try and drive the herd in the wrong direction, perhaps deeper into the Border Marches towards an Uratha pack, perhaps towards a region of Broken Time, but either way it becomes apparent that they are heading towards certain doom. The initiate will have to muster all their willpower and whatever physical strength they have left to break from the herd and lead it, guiding it away from danger. The bull-shape Gudthabak will challenge them- perhaps charging, perhaps with the Ritemaster even striking the initiate, but they must hold firm and change the direction of the herd. In triumph, they are transformed from simply being part of the herd, to being those who lead it. (Stamina + Survival)<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (50 Successes ; Each roll represents 1 hour)<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>The initiate is transformed into a Primal Urge 1 Gudthabak, having shown that they are indeed worthy of guiding the mortal herd and joining the pantheon of Bull's children. They gain their Auspice and their first dot of Renown from the means by which they took control of the herd during the Rite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T13:09:00-07:00","id":870522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=870336#post870336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait- isn't there a theory that the Kereboi of the Ocean of Fragments is actually a Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait what?<br /> <br /> Though to be honest, I felt the Book of the Dead didn't really present a strong coherent theme for the Underworld. I hope 2E does it better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=870404#post870404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) It might be a statistical thing. That is, far, far fewer Chthonians actually WANT to make such a bargain, but in the Neolithic era that matches up with the low population just fine. However, nowadays Geists more or less flood that sort of dealmaking so it appears like they're the only ones that do it. Maybe there ARE Chthonian-Bound in modern times, they're just an incredible rarity? That could be its own interesting antagonist or just mysterious NPC in more modern times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that the Underworld has grown larger over time (I have a grand theory if anyone's interested) so maybe in the Neolithic Chthonians are much closer to the surface.<br /> <br /> As time went on more and more domains cut them off from humans and bargains. Fortunately the more mobile Geists arrived to take their place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T16:06:05-07:00","id":870728,"title":"","content":"So, I shared some of my own thoughts on Neolithic vampires in (appropriately enough) the Vampires in the Neolithic thread, particularly that I liked the idea of the ancestors of the various clans being very different creatures that gradually grew more similar to one another. Along those lines, I thought I might start throwing out some ideas about ancient vampires that are more along those lines.<br /> <br /> So, first off, here's my first crack at a sort of &quot;Proto-Nosferatu&quot;:<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares</b><br /> <br /> Neither immaterial ghosts not entirely things of this world, Nightmares are rarely seen or heard, but are nevertheless known by the fear and sickness that they spread. It is said that they are unclean spirits cast up upon the shores of Ocean Beyond Life, and that they come up from caves and deep wells to prey upon the living. They rarely venture far from the dark holes from which they emerge, for they cannot abide the light of the sun and so go about only at night.<br /> <br /> The Nightmare template consists of the following:<ul><li><b>Face of Horror: </b>Nightmares are frightfully hideous when their true form is revealed. They are said to most commonly resemble rotten and waterlogged human corpses, but they always bear some deformity, like a twisted limb (sometimes in excess of the normal number), a vestigial tail, or a mouth full of jagged and broken fangs, which marks them as not entirely human in origin. A nightmare can never disguise its monstrousness through any mundane means, and is incapable of normal social interaction with humans under most circumstances.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Hunt Unseen: </b>Nightmares are naturally invisible to mortal perception and concealed even from the mystic senses possessed by the Wise. Those among the Wise who are learned in such matters believe that this is an effect of the creatures\u2019 supernatural hideousness; that mortal senses and even the mind\u2019s eye naturally turn away from such horror without registering anything more than a nameless unease. Attempts to penetrate this invisibility using supernatural means trigger a Clash of Wills. A Nightmare can deliberately reveal itself to mortal senses, but this takes a conscious act of will on its part.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Unearthly Form: </b>Nightmares are only partly beings of this world, and are neither living in any ordinary sense of the term nor entirely made up of physical matter. Outside of extraordinary circumstances (at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion), Nightmares suffer no damage from sources of harm that would normally inflict bashing damage, and suffer only bashing damage from sources that would normally deal lethal damage. They suffer Aggravated Damage from fire and sunlight as described in <i>Vampire: the Requiem 2nd Edition.</i> In addition, Nightmares are preternaturally light, weighing no more than a large cat or small dog in spite of their size and strength. They leave no footprints in firm ground and only the faintest traces even on snow or soft mud, and they can stand on top of sleeping victims without harming or waking them.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Predatory Senses: </b>Nightmares have exceptional night vision and generally keen senses. They automatically gain the benefits of the <i>Acute Senses</i> merit and never suffer any die penalties from darkness. They do not, however, have any particular affinity for or special senses related to blood.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Breath-Drinking: </b>Nightmares feed upon the breath of the living, and may only feed from a sleeping or unconscious victims. Although it inflicts damage and the <i>Drained</i> condition as described in <i>Vampire: The Requiem 2nd Edition</i>, the act of feeding does not itself pose a risk of waking the victim. Victims of a Nightmare\u2019s feeding invariably suffer surreal and terrifying dreams which are sometimes recognizable to the Wise as visions of horrors from the Ocean Beyond Life. These dreams, along with the pain and weakness caused by the Nightmare\u2019s feeding, are often the only signs of the creature plaguing the community.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Born of Darkness: </b>Nightmares cannot embrace, nor can they create Ghouls or Revenants. They seem to arise spontaneously from the deep, dark places of the world. Each comes into the world with a Humanity between 3 and 5 and memories of once having been human, but these memories are often distorted and incomplete, and blended with nightmarish visions of a hellish underworld. No Nightmare can remember its death, if indeed it ever did suffer a mortal death, and none can adequately explain how it came to be in its present state. They do not begin play with any touchstones by default, but may gain them by taking the Touchstone merit at character creation or in the course of play.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Vampiric Traits: </b>Nightmares begin play with one dot of Potency, which they may increase through the normal means, although they are incapable of performing Diablerie. They may spend vitae to heal or activate Physical Intensity as described in <i>Vampire: The Requem 2nd Edition</i>. They possess the Predatory Aura, but may only evoke the Monstrous Beast when Lashing Out or fighting another vampire\u2019s Predatory Aura. They suffer the normal consequences of damage, including Torpor. In addition to their basic abilities, Nightmares may purchase the <i>Atrocious</i>, <i>Haven</i>, <i>Touchstone</i>, and <i>Unsettling Gaze</i> merits, and the <i>Celerity</i>, <i>Nightmare</i>, <i>Potence</i>, and <i>Resilience</i> Disciplines, as well as appropriate Devotions.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 04-21-2016, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T21:26:44-07:00","id":870914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=869787#post869787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely like the idea of Kindred Bloodlines emerging from the groups of Revenants and Strix, but I'm also of the opinion that most vampires out there are Revenants. Not too many Kindred out there to do the Embracing, and those that are seem likely to be spawning from the Synthesis Embodiment, and from Neglatu-like Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> I really love the idea of Sin-Eaters in this era making the Bargain with Cthonians- they're probably even more alien than Geists and definitely more eldritch. I imagine the Stygian Key and the Pit Manifestation are a good deal more common. How do you think a Cthonian Bound differs from a Geist Bound?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with Neglatu nests, and Synthesis being things as extension of Revenants and Stryx that may lay foundation for the future Clans. I just don't think anything the Kindred would recognize as Kindred should exist YET, and I definitely think the theme of &quot;hungry dead&quot; rather than anything more sophisticated should guide the presentation of proto-vampires in the era.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Bound are this metaphysically different works well with my LBK concept I think - already dead granted true resurrection through a dangerous rite, as opposed to the near-death experience norm of the Geist-Bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T04:04:49-07:00","id":871096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=870247#post870247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this Era certainly lacks Arisen (and no, I don't like the idea of time travel back before the date of the Rite)...</div> </div> </div> </div>So there's something I finally disagree with you on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:45:12-07:00","id":871625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=871096#post871096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's something I finally disagree with you on</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, what can I say; I like the Rite being a start point, with mummies drifting anywhere between then and thr modern day at the whims of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T13:47:40-07:00","id":871696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=871096#post871096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's something I finally disagree with you on</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My issue with Arisen pre-Irem is thematic. The power of the Arisen speaks to things ancient &amp; lost. Putting them in a context where their power is of the future undermines that. I'd rather come up with something entirely different out of the Judges/Azar/Temahk cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T14:49:46-07:00","id":871749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=871696#post871696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> My issue with Arisen pre-Irem is thematic. The power of the Arisen speaks to things ancient &amp; lost. Putting them in a context where their power is of the future undermines that. I'd rather come up with something entirely different out of the Judges/Azar/Temahk cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>We might try and describe one of the pre-Irem Shan'iatu, back when they were still formless things roaming around the world.<br /> <br /> I think they have odd similarities to the Idigam, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T14:54:29-07:00","id":871755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=870728#post870728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I shared some of my own thoughts on Neolithic vampires in (appropriately enough) the Vampires in the Neolithic thread, particularly that I liked the idea of the ancestors of the various clans being very different creatures that gradually grew more similar to one another. Along those lines, I thought I might start throwing out some ideas about ancient vampires that are more along those lines.<br /> <br /> So, first off, here's my first crack at a sort of &quot;Proto-Nosferatu&quot;:<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares</b> [...] for brevity</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the sort of thing I'd like to see. Something not quite Kindred, but not quite a Revenant phenomenon either, that still gives hints of and resembles the Clans that would later come into existence.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=870914#post870914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the Bound are this metaphysically different works well with my LBK concept I think - already dead granted true resurrection through a dangerous rite, as opposed to the near-death experience norm of the Geist-Bound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell me more about your ideas- I'm really liking the idea of these horrifying, eldritch beings called back from the Ocean Beneath The World, herding and devouring ghosts, living as gods amongst men. It has a very Lovecraftian feel to it and it's so <i>different </i>from Geist in a great way. Still tracking down all references to Cthonians that I can.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> Quick and dirty hacks for the Bull-Shifters and the Distant Ones. Still thinking up a way to summarize the purpose of the Distant Ones. I think it has something to do with foretelling the future and change, but I'm struggling to find a way to phrase it. Nothing snappy like <b>The Wolf Must Hunt </b>or <b>The Bull Guides the Herd </b>comes to mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Children of Bull- The <i>Gudthabak</i>:</b> Glorious and terrible as the Pangaean god that spawned them, they are proud, strong, and supernaturally charismatic. Even a single <i>Gudthabak</i> can bring a village under their sway.<ul><li><b>Systems</b><ul><li>A <i>Gudthabak </i>character gains a dot of the Supernatural Resistance Merit for free, and the Language (First Tongue) Merit for free. Dots in Supernatural Resistance serve as an Honorary Rank.<ul><li><i>Gudthabak</i> characters also commonly possess the Striking Looks (Advanced) Merit and the Biokinesis Merit.</li> </ul></li> <li>A starting Bull-Shifter gains the Skinthief (Aurochs) Merit. Their talisman is Permanent, and is a small totem made either of ivory from Bull\u2019s horns or a fragment of one of Bull\u2019s omphalos stones, traditionally adorned with copper or semiprecious stones and carved into an image of Bull. They gain 20 Experiences to spend on the Skinthief Merit.<ul><li>Common choices include Bare Necessities, Essence Pool, Hybrid Form, Quick Change, and Spirit Powers.<ul><li>Dots in Spirit Powers may be spent on suitably thematic Rites or Dread Powers on a dot-per-dot basis. ST approved Shadow Gift Facets may be purchased as well, with the Bull-Shifter possessing an effective Renown of 1</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>A <i>Gudthabak </i>character may use Fetishes and Talens, and even make them should they possess the appropriate Rite. They may also purchase the Essence Pool Merit a number of times equal to their dots in the Supernatural Resistance Merit.<ul><li>A group of <i>Gudthabak</i> and their \u2018Bull-Blooded\u2019 companions may also purchase the Totem Merit.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><b>The Distant Ones- The <i>Surthu Athilal</i>:</b> The Children of Bird know better. Like their mother, they are swift, wise, and mercurial. The Distant Ones <i>know better</i>- they can see the future coming. They dwell high above the mortals scurrying below, closer to the sky where they can use their significant powers of insight to see what is to come in the flight of birds, the passage of the winds, and the movements of the stars.<ul><li><b>Systems</b><ul><li>A <i>Surthu Athilal</i> character gains a dot of the Supernatural Resistance Merit for free, and the Language (First Tongue) Merit for free. Dots in Supernatural Resistance serve as an Honorary Rank.<ul><li><i>Surthu Athilal </i>characters also commonly possess the Omen Sense Merit and the Clairvoyance Merit.</li> </ul></li> <li>A starting Falcon-God gains the Skinthief (Bird of Prey) Merit. Their talisman is Permanent, and is a small totem made from shreds of Bird\u2019s own molted feathers or a piece of one of Bird\u2019s omphalos stones, strung on a flax cord with natural crystals, shaped into an effigy of Bird herself. They gain 20 Experiences to spend on the Skinthief Merit.<ul><li>Common choices include Strong Instincts, Resilient Form, Twisted Tongue, and Animal Speech.</li> </ul></li> <li>A <i>Surthu Athilal</i> character may use Fetishes and Talens, and even make them should they possess the appropriate Rite. They may also possess the Essence Pool Merit a number of times equal to their dots in the Supernatural Resistance Merit.<ul><li>A group of <i>Surthu Athilal</i> and their \u2018Bird-Blessed\u2019 companions may also purchase the Totem Merit.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-22-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T15:00:20-07:00","id":871761,"title":"","content":"ammm.. a way to play &quot;Mummy&quot; without being a Mummy.. an interesting challenge. Other than playing Sekhem Sorcerers, perhaps there could be some other paths- like primal forms of Lifeless formed from wild Sekhem and shaped from the bones of the world, or perhaps some form of intelligent Amkhata, or an Amkhat which possess a dead body or something like that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T15:04:15-07:00","id":871766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=871761#post871761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ammm.. a way to play &quot;Mummy&quot; without being a Mummy.. an interesting challenge. Other than playing Sekhem Sorcerers, perhaps there could be some other paths- like primal forms of Lifeless formed from wild Sekhem and shaped from the bones of the world, or perhaps some form of intelligent Amkhata, or an Amkhat which possess a dead body or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe Lifeless formed from wild Sekhem, intelligent Amkhata, and Amkhata constructed from the long-dead are all things present in this era and referred to in the first chapter of Book of the Deceived. By this point in time, the Temakh have all been fighting these things, and all been wounded, and all communicated to Ammut. Some have gone to Anpu. They're probably getting close to convening together for the first time in centuries, since Azar is killed sometime around the Sundering.<br /> <br /> So these are definitely things that exist in-setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T23:11:34-07:00","id":872149,"title":"","content":"<u><b>The Purified in the Sundered World</b></u><br /> <br /> Sometimes accidents happen. That's what the purified are, accidents. In the Neolithic, there is only one way for a mortal to become immortal. No magic rite or ritual can delay the onset of age. There is no special potion to kill you and then restore your heartbeat. There is no philosopher stone from which springs the elixir of life. To become Purified three things must happen. First, you must have some skill with the occult. Second, you must travel into the Shadow. Finally, and most importantly, while in the <u>Shadow</u> you must be devoured by a Pangaean. Naturally, only a very few who meet these requirements ever come back as the Purified, but those who do are imbued with a fraction of the power of the mighty Pangaean that consumed them.<br /> <br /> As occult knowledge is required to become Purified, and hedge magic aids the process, The People who do become Purified are often drawn from the ranks of those who associate with The Wise or from the Wolf-born. Typically, this means that most Purified are potters or hunters.<br /> <br /> The People have no name for the Purified. The chances of meeting even one of the Purified is extremely small to begin with, and even those individuals who encounter them mistake them for the Wise. Some of the Wise are aware of their existence, although there is no standard nomenclature for the Purified yet, so a variety of names like The Returned, Spirit-Cousins, and Clay-Shapers are used. In the First Tongue, the Purified are known as the Asilal-thakh, or &quot;Distant Wanderers&quot;. Wolf-born will occasionally go on a hunt for Urfarah, hoping to that Mother Wolf's hungry jaws offer them a different path to power than that of the Uratha. Most die horrible, mundane deaths and many Purified never find Father Wolf, instead returning with another Pangaean as their arcane totem.<br /> <br /> <b>Creating a Neolithic Purified Character</b><br /> <br /> When creating a Neolithic Purified Character, the normal Purified template in Immortals is amended as follows:<ul><li>In addition to having access to Numina and Siddhi, the Purified have access to a single Arcana, which is chosen at character creation. This Arcana is always the highest Arcana possessed by the Pangaean that created them. The Purified may purchase spells from that Arcana on a dot-for-dot basis, just as the Proximi of later eras do. The Purified use Chi in place of Gnosis, Integrity in place of Wisdom, and may spend Essence instead of Mana when casting spells.</li> <li>The Purified's Unseen Sense applies the Pangaean that created the Purified and to any evidence of their passage, even if that evidence is entirely mundane in nature. The Purified have a deep spiritual connection to their progenitors, so they know if they have crossed through the fields where Bull was grazing yesterday, or if they pass over the site of Fox's demise.</li> </ul><b>What has yet to come: </b><br /> <br /> Just as the worlds of the Wise and the Urathra are destined to be thrown into upheaval by the death of Wolf, the Purified will be dramatically impacted as well. With the fall of Pangaea and the rise of the Gauntlet, the Asilal-thakh find their souls split in half. They have the ability to draw upon both the Shadow and the Supernal; the latter connection is primarily mediated through their connection with the Pangaeans. Through the magic of sympathy, even a dead Pangaean can sustain a Purified's magic, largely thanks to the existence of the Omphalos Stones. The Gauntlet seals many Pangaeans away, however, cutting off the Purified's contact with their spiritual anchors. Many Purified cope the same way that the remaining Pangaeans do, by shedding their connection to the Arcana. Others trade immortality for power, gaining access to a second Arcana and becoming the first Proximi. A rare few continue to strike a balance between the spiritual and Supernal, but they all but disappear when the Vinca culture is finally destroyed.<br /> <br /> *******<br /> <br /> A pretty simple adaptation, but I really like it. I'm sure there are things that we can pick apart and improve, but I think this fits nicely into the weirdness niche of the Sundered World without being too over the top in terms of power. There are some fun implications and seeds that I thought up of while writing. In particular, I'd like to know what happens to the Wolf-born who was purified by Bull when the <b><i>Gudthabak</i></b> come calling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 04-23-2016, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T01:35:33-07:00","id":872215,"title":"","content":"This is definitely an interesting tweak to the Purified for a Neolithic setting. Especially tying them to the Proximi as (perhaps) the first of their number.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, I do wonder how this 'hack' could apply in a modern setting, though. It'd be quite the Mystery for modern Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T06:38:52-07:00","id":872322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=871696#post871696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue with Arisen pre-Irem is thematic. The power of the Arisen speaks to things ancient &amp; lost. Putting them in a context where their power is of the future undermines that. I'd rather come up with something entirely different out of the Judges/Azar/Temahk cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no.<br /> <br /> Yes, the power of the Arisen is ancient, lost, and arguably (not really arguable, actually) dwindling. They are cursed to not only be servants but they're cursed to be immortal. The world will only grow increasingly alien as they struggle to adapt. The art of relic creation is lost, the number of Shuankhsen only increases, the power mortal sorcerers wield diminishes, and people forsake the divine entirely. Despite their everlasting nature they're doomed.<br /> <br /> But no, because underneath it all is a sense of <i>timelessness</i>. In every civilization for literally all of history the Deathless see the branches grown from the Nameless Empire's deep roots. Every myth hearkens back to theirs. The magic of Utterances is classic, Biblical myth kind of stuff that doesn't grow old. Death ever weighs heavy on the mortal mind, influencing them to join death cults no matter which age they dwell.<br /> <br /> Sekhem is the lifeblood of the material world. It's been there since the first woman laid eyes on her child, and since a son set his dying mother to rest. Death is timeless. Lifeless things abound in the Sundered World.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in all that is a story to be told, whether or not our protagonists are Mummies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:39:10-07:00","id":872450,"title":"","content":"Except the whole slavery narrative of their state of being doesn't work in an era before slavery and imperialism. It's not a matter of it growing old, it's not born yet. Sure Lifeless things abound, but not the Arisen, and not their powers that speak to the sorcerous glories of the Nameless Empire.<br /> <br /> The narrative of Death and Resurrection is timeless, which is why we have the Bound, not to mention Revenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:45:15-07:00","id":872455,"title":"","content":"something I've thought about.<br /> <br /> Mummy has always had at least a bit of Lovecraftian atmosphere, with beings called from beneath the world or beyond the stars or creatures like poisoned one or what's her face from the Deceived book. That made me thinking- yes, in such era there is no place in human history for stories of ancient glories, long years and immortal souls...<br /> <br /> but what about inhuman history?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T13:17:03-07:00","id":872606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=872455#post872455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something I've thought about.<br /> <br /> Mummy has always had at least a bit of Lovecraftian atmosphere, with beings called from beneath the world or beyond the stars or creatures like poisoned one or what's her face from the Deceived book. That made me thinking- yes, in such era there is no place in human history for stories of ancient glories, long years and immortal souls...<br /> <br /> but what about inhuman history?</div> </div> </div> </div>Irem has not yet named and tamed the stars above, allowing them to freely wander the sky. Horrors like the angels of the Black Huriyah and demons like the Ochre-Masked King or Herald of Forgotten Stars wreak ruin on yhe world unopposed. The Shan'iatu themselves are wild, shapeless, and incredibly powerful, and Ammut has always hungered.<br /> <br /> While the first pillars have yet to rise out of the black land, the monsters that the Nameless Empire triumphed over have yet to be bound and broken, leaving the world a horrifically dangerous place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T13:35:39-07:00","id":872614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=872215#post872215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is definitely an interesting tweak to the Purified for a Neolithic setting. Especially tying them to the Proximi as (perhaps) the first of their number.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note, I do wonder how this 'hack' could apply in a modern setting, though. It'd be quite the Mystery for modern Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's doable, mostly likely in a chronicle where Pangaea or the Pangaeans returned. It could also be an interesting hook if a Proximus family found a way to created a Purified that still could access Arcana but without their family curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T16:48:32-07:00","id":872729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=872614#post872614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's doable, mostly likely in a chronicle where Pangaea or the Pangaeans returned. It could also be an interesting hook if a Proximus family found a way to created a Purified that still could access Arcana but without their family curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, speaking of Pangaea returning, I've been trying to work out ideas for making the Border Marches exist in a modern setting, albeit <i>heavily</i> diminished and fragmented. The Shatter from Mirrors' Woundgate setting is currently my starting ref for, but it's still slow-going.<br /> <br /> On a more related note to this thread, the sidebar for other splats in the Sundered World makes mention of Changelings. And how they are still victims of abduction even in that Era. Which made me wonder how Arc's ideas on the Huntsmen being top dogs could still work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:49:29-07:00","id":872853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=872729#post872729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more related note to this thread, the sidebar for other splats in the Sundered World makes mention of Changelings. And how they are still victims of abduction even in that Era. Which made me wonder how Arc's ideas on the Huntsmen being top dogs could still work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the chapter mentions people being carried off to a &quot;labyrinth of thorns,&quot; which implies that the Others are already lurking in the Hedge; it doesn't mean, however, what if they're already the masters of Arcadia. Perhaps the Arcadia of the Sundered World is a wild, masterless place where the Huntsmen and other fluid, formless beings thrive. Maybe the first Gentry are just beginning to learn how to tame the chaos from which they emerged by observing the development of agricultural civilization, and the way in which mere mortals are gradually transforming a hostile wilderness into fields and pastures that serve their needs. These one-day conquerors might haunt the Hedge and in the dreams of mortals, dwelling as close to the unchanging world of matter as they can stand, launching occasional forays to collect some castoff bauble or isolated individual that arouses their curiosity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 04-23-2016, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T21:16:29-07:00","id":872868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=872853#post872853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the chapter mentions people being carried off to a &amp;quot;labyrinth of thorns,&amp;quot; which implies that the Others are already lurking in the Hedge; it doesn't mean, however, what if they're already the masters of Arcadia. Perhaps the Arcadia of the Sundered World is a wild, masterless place where the Huntsmen and other fluid, formless beings thrive. Maybe the first Gentry are just beginning to learn how to tame the chaos from which they emerged by observing the development of agricultural civilization, and the way in which mere mortals are gradually transforming a hostile wilderness into fields and pastures that serve their needs. These one-day conquerors might haunt the Hedge and in the dreams of mortals, dwelling as close to the unchanging world of matter as they can stand, launching occasional forays to collect some castoff bauble or isolated individual that arouses their curiosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And maybe the Huntsmen of this Era were more akin to Gentry in the sense that perhaps they could also transform people into changelings? Perhaps, as the Others rise into ascendancy, this is an ability that the Huntsmen lose as they are forced into the state they are in at modern times?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T00:04:05-07:00","id":872934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=872729#post872729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a more related note to this thread, the sidebar for other splats in the Sundered World makes mention of Changelings. And how they are still victims of abduction even in that Era. Which made me wonder how Arc's ideas on the Huntsmen being top dogs could still work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've elected to ignore that as it doesn't provide anything different about Changelings &amp; Gentry in the era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T00:50:26-07:00","id":872953,"title":"","content":"Regarding the True Fae, we have to ask &quot;who made the Contract(s)&quot; that allowed them to abduct humans? This is so early that the Contract might not have happened yet, or it might only affect some places until &quot;all my descendants&quot; spreads across humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T03:11:26-07:00","id":872985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=872953#post872953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the True Fae, we have to ask &amp;quot;who made the Contract(s)&amp;quot; that allowed them to abduct humans? This is so early that the Contract might not have happened yet, or it might only affect some places until &amp;quot;all my descendants&amp;quot; spreads across humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember an idea mentioned in another thread that suggested that the Contract which allowed the Fae to abduct humans may have been made to protect Humanity from the Huntsmen. Can't remember the details beyond that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T03:24:21-07:00","id":872990,"title":"","content":"I believe it was my idea, which I wrote in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/857526-neolithic-era-for-everyone?p=858367#post858367\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T04:00:07-07:00","id":873008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=872990#post872990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it was my idea, which I wrote in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/857526-neolithic-era-for-everyone?p=858367#post858367&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes it is.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, this could be interesting to build on in a Neolithic setting for so many reasons, seeing as the hunter vs. farmer clash takes on a more <i>literal</i> note when you pit Huntsmen and Gentry together. Especially when both entities are capable of making changelings to reinforce their respective narrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T05:12:19-07:00","id":873019,"title":"","content":"Having read <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>'s idea I propose a slight variation. Rather than the Huntsmen adopting those lost babies and setting them against their old community, I propose the lost babies came first. They were ordinary feral children who led wolf packs (and similar) and caused a nuisance to humanity because that's what wolves do.<br /> <br /> Over time the stories told about this children assigned them all sorts of strange powers, because lets face it, children leading packs of wolves are a bit freaky. These stories gradually made the children into fae - and also restored their intelligence to human like levels because in the stories they're smart. There's precedent for this already actually. Legend Slashers. Though these children aren't nessacarally motivated by murder as an end to itself, different stories.<br /> <br /> When the actual kids died the stories lived on, eventually becoming independent Huntsmen in their own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T05:21:54-07:00","id":873022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=872606#post872606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irem has not yet named and tamed the stars above, allowing them to freely wander the sky. Horrors like the angels of the Black Huriyah and demons like the Ochre-Masked King or Herald of Forgotten Stars wreak ruin on yhe world unopposed. The Shan'iatu themselves are wild, shapeless, and incredibly powerful, and Ammut has always hungered.<br /> <br /> While the first pillars have yet to rise out of the black land, the monsters that the Nameless Empire triumphed over have yet to be bound and broken, leaving the world a horrifically dangerous place.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a surprising amount of playable characters in <b>Mummy </b>that are more than typical mortals: Witnesses, mortal sorcerers, Lucid ghosts, and sadikh.<br /> <br /> And then yeah. An unsurprising amount of blood-drinking, flesh-rending monsters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T13:28:41-07:00","id":873250,"title":"","content":"I've kind of operated on a presumption that the city the Pain Profit mentions may have been Atlantis. This idea, and the idea that time was changed. It was the 2nd children that populated earth, the beastial ones, the children of the Dark Mother. Humans remember a long history but that doesn't mean it happened, or it did (time changes). This is why I think that certain things should only now be starting to form. The 2nd children are only now integrating themselves with the third children.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=868594#post868594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if I'll join but I can see a way that demon's could work.<br /> A) The first angel(s) of the machine to fall.<br /> B) Demon(s) thrown through time and having to hide in a time the machine may not even exist but it's best to not test your luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe something to do with Lucifer, not all Angels are happy with the Fall and question God.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T13:48:04-07:00","id":873257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=873250#post873250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've kind of operated on a presumption that the city the Pain Profit mentions may have been Atlantis. This idea, and the idea that time was changed. It was the 2nd children that populated earth, the beastial ones, the children of the Dark Mother. Humans remember a long history but that doesn't mean it happened, or it did (time changes). This is why I think that certain things should only now be starting to form. The 2nd children are only now integrating themselves with the third children.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe something to do with Lucifer, not all Angels are happy with the Fall and question God.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>D:tD doesn't really have a Lucifer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T13:53:23-07:00","id":873261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=873257#post873257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> D:tD doesn't really have a Lucifer.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is more accurate to say that the unchained have lucifer as a myth and are uncertain if he was a demon. (See: lucifer fell like lightning)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T14:26:44-07:00","id":873285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=873261#post873261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is more accurate to say that the unchained have lucifer as a myth and are uncertain if he was a demon. (See: lucifer fell like lightning)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> which book is this in?<br /> <br /> That said I see this as a time where myths aren't so mythical and yet may be different from what people remember (Father wolf is alive, Atlantis is real, etc, AFAIK these are both myth's in 2e)<br /> <br /> I'm thinking the whole Era is really about paradise lost, thus the Garden of Eden myth might go perfectly into this era, except some things should be changed and not what the bible says. Perhaps lucifer is in cover as a snake and needs to convince eve to get a body. I had this idea that maybe the God Machine is actually offline (or experiencing some post Fall malfunction) and Lucifer has yet to fall, instead stuck in serpent form he has to convince Eve to restart the system. Later Lucifer sees what the Machine has become and falls. Then again maybe eden should be seen as even before this (or after). This could be an event during this period.<br /> <br /> Just throwing out some idea's for Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T14:35:47-07:00","id":873293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=873285#post873285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> which book is this in?<br /> <br /> That said I see this as a time where myths aren't so mythical and yet may be different from what people remember (Father wolf is alive, Atlantis is real, etc, AFAIK these are both myth's in 2e)<br /> <br /> I'm thinking the whole Era is really about paradise lost, thus the Garden of Eden myth might go perfectly into this era, except some things should be changed and not what the bible says. Perhaps lucifer is in cover as a snake and needs to convince eve to get a body. I had this idea that maybe the God Machine is actually offline (or experiencing some post Fall malfunction) and Lucifer has yet to fall, instead stuck in serpent form he has to convince Eve to restart the system. Later Lucifer sees what the Machine has become and falls. Then again maybe eden should be seen as even before this (or after). This could be an event during this period.<br /> <br /> Just throwing out some idea's for Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is in the core for demon the decent starts on page 38. Though looking through it, it seems to be the title for a separate title. I'm certain however that there was more to it I just can't seem to find it right now.<br /> <br /> It was an off hand mention either way. A rumour none took serious in the fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T15:00:04-07:00","id":873315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=873293#post873293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is in the core for demon the decent starts on page 38. Though looking through it, it seems to be the title for a separate title.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Bible quote. Luke 10:18.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T17:42:50-07:00","id":873408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=873285#post873285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking the whole Era is really about paradise lost, thus the Garden of Eden myth might go perfectly into this era, except some things should be changed and not what the bible says. Perhaps lucifer is in cover as a snake and needs to convince eve to get a body. I had this idea that maybe the God Machine is actually offline (or experiencing some post Fall malfunction) and Lucifer has yet to fall, instead stuck in serpent form he has to convince Eve to restart the system. Later Lucifer sees what the Machine has become and falls. Then again maybe eden should be seen as even before this (or after). This could be an event during this period.</div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;paradise lost&quot; is the theme, I think a relevant question would be &quot;whose paradise?&quot; The Chronicles of Darkness stone age is a hard time to be a mortal, even when compared with all the supernatural dangers of the Chronicles of Darkness modern era. Under the leadership of the Wise, the People are building a better world for themselves out of the bones of the dying hunter's paradise.<br /> <br /> Assuming the God Machine is around and active already, the real question is which side it's on. Is the Machine subtly promoting the emergence of agricultural societies in order to weaken it's supernatural rivals and cultivating mankind into a more useful resource, or has the neolithic revolution thrown off some vast and ancient plan in which humanity was meant to play little or no part? If it's the former, would that make the Demons of the neolithic enemies of humanity and allies of the more misanthropic factions of Uratha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T17:48:48-07:00","id":873412,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post, but I wanted to respond to xenoterracide and I figured I should separate this out. I've put together some ideas for a Proto-Mekhet template; I might have gone a bit overboard with the fluff on this one, but I'd love to know what people think:<br /> <br /> <b>Hollow Ones</b><br /> <br /> Throughout the villages of the People, elder hunters and well-traveled traders share stories of the Hollow One. The story always begins the same way, with a traveler who becomes separated from their companions somewhere deep in the wilderness. Perhaps they fell into a swift-moving stream and were carried away faster than their fellows could follow, or into a ravine to steep to be safely descended. In some versions of the story, the traveler is snatched up by some horror that sends their companions fleeing, and are abandoned to their fate.<br /> <br /> In any case, the traveler is left for dead, with no grave or funeral to set their spirit to rest. The traveler\u2019s companions return home and tell the story of their lost companion, and the community mourns but can do no more. In time, the mourning period passes, and life continues much as it always has; travel is very dangerous, after all, and such tragedies are hardly unheard of.<br /> <br /> And then, one night, when the moon is new and the stars are covered by clouds, the traveler returns, seemingly alive and whole. At first the community is reluctant to embrace the traveler, for ghosts and worse things have been known to take the body or likeness of a loved one in order to work evil in a village of the people. But the traveler knows their friends and loved ones, and seems at first unchanged, if confused and troubled by their ordeal, and before the night is through they are joyfully embraced once more by their family, even if other villagers still have misgivings.<br /> <br /> When the traveler sleeps like a stone through the whole of the next day, their loved ones make little of it. They had traveled far in the night, and had gone long without the comforts of a roof and sleeping-mat. Soon, however, it seems as if the traveler has contracted some strange sickness, for each day they remain as still as a corpse, and each night they rise complaining of hunger but unable to keep down any food that is given to them. The light of fire hurts their eyes, and they take to wandering in dark places, creeping silently while they mouthe a constant stream of soundless babble to themselves. When confronted about these lonely sojourns, the traveler reacts with the dazed confusion of a sleepwalker, and cannot remember what possessed them to behave so strangely.<br /> <br /> The traveler\u2019s family consults with one of the Wise who lives in the village, a young willworker on the Path of Blood, but neither medicine nor magic seems to provide any relief for their condition. Before long, however, someone close to the traveler discovers something that no amount of wishful thinking can explain away. In some versions of the story, the traveler\u2019s spouse follows them in secret on one of their somnambulant rambles, only to find the traveler bent over the body of some small beast, sucking desperately at a ragged hole in its throat with hot blood dripping down their chin. In others, a friend comes to call on a night when the moon is clear and bright, and gradually comes to to the horrifying realization that the traveler casts no shadow in the pale light.<br /> <br /> The traveler\u2019s family fears that the traveler has been possessed or claimed by some baleful spirit, and the traveler offers no resistance when they are brought before the local Wise. Although the holy man can offer no promises of salvation, he agrees to examine the traveler in order to determine the nature of their condition. What the Wise One discovers horrifies him, for while he can find no spirit nor sign of spiritual claiming, when he peers into the soul of the afflicted traveler he sees only a hungry darkness staring back at him. In his shock he turns upon the traveler with a burning brand, and to his surprise the traveler suddenly vanishes from his sight.<br /> <br /> For many nights thereafter, the people of the village hear the forlorn wailing of the Hollow One, emerging from the darkness beyond the reach of the furthest hearth fire.The family of the traveler is left to mourn once more, and none dare venture beyond the lights of the village until the wailing has at last grown distant enough that it no longer troubles the sleep of the living.<br /> <br /> <br /> As with many such tales, versions of the story of the Hollow One is far more common in the lands of the People than the creatures which they describe. Hollow Ones are a rare sort of walking corpse, little understood even by the Wise who study such creatures. Like many others of their ilk, the Hollow Ones arise from the bodies of the abandoned dead and hunger for the flesh and blood of the living, but they are marked by many peculiarities. Many, like the Hollow One in the story above, do not fully understand the nature of their condition, and strive to return to some semblance of their former life. This never ends well for them.<br /> <br /> The Hollow One template consists of the following:<ul><li><b>A Sleep Like Death:</b> Unlike certain other, similar beings Hollow Ones are not physically harmed by sunlight, but this doesn\u2019t mean that they can go about freely during the day. From Dawn until Dusk, a Hollow One slips into a dormant state indistinguishable from death. The creature\u2019s illusion of humanity slips away, and through the daylight hours it resembles nothing more than a corpse, if a strangely well-preserved one. While resting in this state, Hollow Ones are invariably troubled by vivid and surreal dreams. A few learn to interpret these strange visions, and gain seemingly impossible insights into other times and places.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Feeding:</b> The Hollow Ones require the blood of the living to maintain their undead state, and there is nothing elegant or subtle about the way in which they feed. They Possess no fangs, and in order to feed they must either incapacitate or immobilize their target and then inflict enough bite attacks to start dealing lethal damage. Once blood is drawn, the Hollow One can feed as described in Vampire: the Requiem 2nd Edition, but their bite confers neither the Scarred nor the Swooning condition, and they have no ability to close the wounds their feeding inflicts. Most Hollow Ones can feed on animals, but more potent bloodsuckers may require human or even supernatural blood.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Hungry Darkness:</b> The darkness that fills the wounds in a Hollow One\u2019s soul is an animate, hungry thing, but it is patient and subtle compared to the Beast that resides in the heart of every modern Kindred. Hollow Ones are not subject to Frenzy, but creature inside of them threatens to take control when it is not adequately fed. The triggers and roll to resist this condition are the same as those for a hunger frenzy as described in Vampire: the Requiem 2nd Edition, save that the Hollow One also risks losing control any time it wakes with two or fewer vitae. When overcome with hunger, a Hollow One gains no bonuses to physical rolls, but adds her Potency to any rolls related to stalking and capturing prey.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Imitation of Life:</b> During the night, Hollow Ones are superficially indistinguishable from living humans, although this can change as the creature ages. Although they have no need to carry out the normal processes of biological life, they still breathe and their heart keeps beating, if at a constant, measured pace. It\u2019s a cherade, of course, a sort of instinctual prey mimicry combined with memories of true life. The illusion is fragile, as well: Hollow Ones do not bleed when cut or bruise when struck, have no need to excrete, and cannot perform sexually. Their body is cool to the touch, and they cannot consume more than a little food without becoming violently ill and emptying their stomach in a hideous and bloody manner. A Hollow One might be able to pass as a very ill human, for a time, but their disguise doesn\u2019t stand up to prolonged scrutiny.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Mimicry:</b> Perhaps as a consequence of their keen senses, Hollow Ones are blessed with an uncanny talent for mimicry. If given the opportunity to closely observe a subject for at least an hour, the Hollow One can thereafter flawlessly imitate the subject\u2019s voice, manner of speech, and physical mannerisms. This does not allow a Hollow One to actually change their physical appearance, but it does grant a +2 bonus to Subterfuge related to disguise.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Preternatural Senses:</b> One of the most distinctive characteristics of the Hollow Ones is the acuity if their senses, which extend far beyond the capabilities of any physical sense organ. They gain all of the benefits of Kindred Senses and the Acute Senses merit, as described in Vampire: the Requiem 2nd edition, and additionally never suffer any die penalties from darkness. Additionally, they can sense the presence of ghosts and other beings in Twilight, although this ability is not precise enough to determine a being\u2019s exact location. A Hollow One can distinguish a supernatural being from an ordinary mortal with a successful Wits + Composure roll, although they must still taste the subject\u2019s blood in order to learn any specific or detailed information about their nature.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Wandering Shadow:</b> The Hollow Ones cast no shadows, nor do they possess reflections or echoes, and they leave no footprints no matter how soft the ground. The Wise believe that the Hollow Ones have lost some crucial part of themselves, leaving a metaphysical \u201chole\u201d in their being which has been filled with shadows and otherworldly whispers. In this they are more right than they know, for this \u201cmissing piece\u201d is both real and active, a ghostly double that is forced to restlessly wander the earth for as long as the Hollow One remains, endlessly hungry and hateful. These spirits manifest as shadows cast by flame or reflections cast in stagnant ponds, and can feed on carrion and other rotting organic matter despite lacking a physical form.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>The Lonely Rebirth:</b> Hollow Ones cannot embrace, nor can they create Ghouls or Revenants. When a Hollow One\u2019s ghostly double encounters an unburied but relatively intact human corpse, it will sometimes attempt to enter the body as if it were a possessing ghost or spirit. Its reasons for doing this are mysterious to those few who are aware of the origin of the Hollow Ones, but the result is always the same: the first ghost emerges, followed shortly by an incorporeal double of the deceased. At the beginning of the following night the body arises as a Hollow One, possessing the memories it had in life but no knowledge of its new nature or how it was created. Bodies which have been ritually consecrated by any sort of formal funerary rite seem to be immune to this transformation unless they have first been deliberately desecrated in some way, even if the body is not physically buried.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Vampiric Traits: </b>Hollow Ones suffer damage and the consequences thereof in the same manner as the Kindred. They may spend vitae to heal or activate Physical Intensity, but they do not have a Predatory Aura and cannot Lash Out. They begin with and can gain Touchstones as normal, and begin with 7 Humanity at character creation. In addition to their basic abilities, Hollow Ones may purchase the Bloodhound, Distinguished Palate, Dream Vision, Haven, and Touchstone merits, and the Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, Potence, and Resilience Disciplines, as well as appropriate Devotions.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T18:18:37-07:00","id":873427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=873408#post873408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If &quot;paradise lost&quot; is the theme, I think a relevant question would be &quot;whose paradise?&quot; The Chronicles of Darkness stone age is a hard time to be a mortal, even when compared with all the supernatural dangers of the Chronicles of Darkness modern era. Under the leadership of the Wise, the People are building a better world for themselves out of the bones of the dying hunter's paradise.<br /> <br /> Assuming the God Machine is around and active already, the real question is which side it's on. Is the Machine subtly promoting the emergence of agricultural societies in order to weaken it's supernatural rivals and cultivating mankind into a more useful resource, or has the neolithic revolution thrown off some vast and ancient plan in which humanity was meant to play little or no part? If it's the former, would that make the Demons of the neolithic enemies of humanity and allies of the more misanthropic factions of Uratha?</div> </div> </div> </div>well in the Dark Eras book, it goes into the Uratha's paradise being lost, and how recent the fall was and the evidence is still around. It blatantly says humanity has lost its rightful place.<br /> <br /> As far as which side the GM is on... what side is it on now? I mean piggy backs on human infrastructure. If the story of the pain profit is to be believed then of course it'd want the human infrastructure. I don't know that it means that the Machine is generally speaking on our side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T04:12:01-07:00","id":873657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=873427#post873427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> well in the Dark Eras book, it goes into the Uratha's paradise being lost, and how recent the fall was and the evidence is still around. It blatantly says humanity has lost its rightful place. As far as which side the GM is on... what side is it on now? I mean piggy backs on human infrastructure. If the story of the pain profit is to be believed then of course it'd want the human infrastructure. I don't know that it means that the Machine is generally speaking on our side.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't say that it's on our side per se. It's more accurate to think that the Machine is concerned with maintaining the status quo of reality in the most efficient manner. The rise of Humanity in the Neolithic Era paired with the Fall of the Time Before and the Sundering of Pangaea would have left it one very logical course of action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T07:17:48-07:00","id":873734,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth pointing out that the Fall of Mage is always in the distant past. The Time Before always was/never had been/is/will be. It only appears more recent because Ruins of the Time Before are bigger and there are fewer Sleepers to wear them down with Dissonance. The Sundering is a measurable event, the Fall isn't due to Imperial Mysteries shenanigans.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3209\" data-vbnamecard=\"3209\">CatDoom</a> I absolutely love your vampire writeups, they really capture the feel of the Clans while remaining their own unique phenomena. I think I like the Hollow Ones the most so far, just because they are so thematic and bizarre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-25-2016, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T05:33:30-07:00","id":874435,"title":"","content":"Anybody have ideas to contribute for a Lodge patronized by the Eater of Names? Granted, I envisioned them as a Lodge that persisted into modern times. Or maybe even a minor Tribe. But I can definitely see them present in the Sundered World Chronicles, <i>especially</i> as antagonists to the Wise for their Reaping of Pangaean souls.<br /> <br /> Here's the Blessing I thought up for them. Arcanist, if you could be so kind as to post the two Facets I PM'd to you, I would appreciate it. I'm also open for ideas on how to handle the Honor, Purity, and Wisdom Facets.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Eaters of Names benefit from the 8-again rule on all Facets of the Scourging Gift, and gain an Exceptional Success with them at three successes instead of five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:58:45-07:00","id":874965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=874435#post874435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anybody have ideas to contribute for a Lodge patronized by the Eater of Names? Granted, I envisioned them as a Lodge that persisted into modern times. Or maybe even a minor Tribe. But I can definitely see them present in the Sundered World Chronicles, <i>especially</i> as antagonists to the Wise for their Reaping of Pangaean souls.<br /> <br /> Here's the Blessing I thought up for them. Arcanist, if you could be so kind as to post the two Facets I PM'd to you, I would appreciate it. I'm also open for ideas on how to handle the Honor, Purity, and Wisdom Facets.<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The Eaters of Names benefit from the 8-again rule on all Facets of the Scourging Gift, and gain an Exceptional Success with them at three successes instead of five.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad I'm not the only one with this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:00:06-07:00","id":875167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=874965#post874965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad I'm not the only one with this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>The feeling's mutual.<br /> <br /> Now, what would the Aspiration and Ban for this Lodge be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:16:49-07:00","id":875294,"title":"","content":"Some random drabble...<br /> <br /> -+-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Those Who Dream</u></b><br /> Though most of the surviving Pangaeans lived on as ethereal spirits or physical Horrors, some escaped the Sundering by other means. These primal gods chose to flee into the Temenos, sacrificing their earthly forms in order to live on as creatures of the Dream. In doing so, they retained their ties to the Arcana, and learned how to shape the world through the collective dreams of Humanity. These Pangaeans would go on to become conceptual gods found in and around the Soul of the World. Some would even immerse themselves in the Dream's most primordial depths, where they would undergo another transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T23:37:35-07:00","id":875357,"title":"","content":"I would never suggest this should be Mummy canon (as it's basically giving one gamelines' cosmology supremacy over another, which never plays well), but IN A SUNDERED WORLD GAME, I'm kind of inclined to have &quot;River&quot; and &quot;Desert&quot; as rival brother Pangeans worshipped in North Africa... and &quot;River&quot; is served by shapeshifting animal demigods, who are being whispered to by &quot;Desert&quot; about turning on their master.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:38:36-07:00","id":875620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=874965#post874965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad I'm not the only one with this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, first I'd suggest developing their patron and philosophy. Why do they hunt Mages? Do they regard them as their Sacred Prey out of respect or hatred? What is Eater of Names like? Does he or she have any sort of quirks thaf suggest something to use? How are the neolithic and modern versions of the Lodge different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T21:03:26-07:00","id":877293,"title":"","content":"I'll be diving into some serious research in the following week. Both in regards to real world Neolithic cultures, and facets of the CofD, so I should have something substantial to provide.<br /> <br /> I'm going to take a stab at making Sin-Eaters a microtemplate based off of the Medium Merit, and get to work on Beasts. I've got ideas on how they operate in this world and how they relate to the Pangaeans, especially the great gods of the Vinca.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T15:45:42-07:00","id":879059,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post, but I have some preliminary stuff on the Neolithic Beasts amongst the Vinca that I wanted to get out.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <b>Begotten Sons and Daughters</b><br /> <br /> Fear was the first language. Before words or even the relatively complex gesture-based vocabulary of the great apes, there was fear. Terror was the best teacher, and the lesson it taught was survival. Screams in the darkness reminded our earliest ancestors that it was best not to look into it, that staying together was the best bet for our continued existence. By the time of the Sundered World, the Primordial Dream is already fairly removed from general humanity, the development of language creating a buffer that pushed it up against the Anima Mundi. There are no recorded legends from this time, no stories of the monsters that haunted their nightmares, but fear of the dragon has always preceded the existence of one. Chambers in the Primordial Dream are born from the trauma of lost Integrity inflicted by a supernatural being, but Horrors and the Hearts of Lairs are born when time, fear, and storytelling allows that trauma to warp, to aggrandize, to <i>teach</i>. That hunter, trader, or lost wanderer made it back to their people and spread the story, and it changed in the telling. The Horrors wait just outside the light of the campfire, and the negative reinforcement of the terror and trauma of a few pulls the community closer together.<br /> <br /> By the time of the Sundered World, it had been nearly 193 000 years since our earliest relatives were born. 193 000 years to encounter Spirits, Restless Dead, and even the gods of the Border Marches. 193 000 years for Horrors to fester and grow. The Horrors are legion, waiting to feast, slumbering in the womb-egg-homes of their Hearts, and they are needed. Mother is calling, because the People are forgetting. They are forgetting fear, they are forgetting that simplest, first lesson. They are forgetting that there is a <i>reason </i>they are afraid of the dark. They look at their villages and hearth fires, they listen to the Wise, they gaze upon their fields, and they think they are safe. They have appeased the spirits of river and flame, they deal with the spirits of field and forest, they beat back the spirits of hunger and disease. They would wander out into the darkness, and they would see what lives there. The People would be devoured by what is waiting.<br /> <br /> Mother speaks: <i>Teach them. Show them fear. Remind them of what they have forgotten. Make them wise.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Here Be Dragons</b><br /> <br /> In the Sundered World, the Primordial Dream isn't quite so restricted and festering, the Bright Dream hasn't expanded far enough to crush it up against the Soul of the World. Communities and populations are small, still in keeping within the limits of how our brains define 'personhood'. We are equipped to handle about 150-200 people as actual living breathing human beings, and anything beyond that effectively becomes background noise. As populations expand, the Primordial Dream becomes cluttered by this static, to the point where only the Children and those who dream deep can even hear it anymore. Not in this age.<br /> <br /> In this age, the Dream is like a clear still pool with horribly dark depths- dreamers can see how deep it goes, the Horrors can find them with much less trouble. Because of this, it becomes far, far easier for one of the Begotten to feed. Any Beast character may feed by <b>Inflicting Nightmares (Beast: The Primordial pg. 99) </b>at any Satiety level voluntarily after successfully meditating, not just involuntarily while asleep when Ravenous or Starving. (Though that still happens) As a result, Neolithic Beasts tend to feed by Inflicting Nightmares while at High Satiety, and indulge their Hungers physically at Low Satiety. Those Begotten who still live in or around their communities tend to feed by Inflicting Nightmares, but are almost invariably driven away by Heroes or the Wise eventually. Most Neolithic Beasts have likely spent some time in the wilderness, fasting down to Ravenous or Starving as they make their way to a new community. Established Children, and especially Apexes or Beasts Incarnate, will often live near, but outside, a village of some kind- their powerful Lairs expanding their hunting grounds in the Dream.<br /> <br /> Because the Bright Dream is so relatively small in this era, and the Primordial Dream so expansive, the Horrors are farther reaching- counting the Temenos in general (outside of specific, human-related, Realms) as part of the Hive. What this translates to is the Begotten being able to take the form of their Horror outside of the Lair while wandering the Dream. The Forest-Wise will often stumble across the Children while roaming the far reaches of the Dream, and some even bargain with them for knowledge of how to sing to the Navel Stone and enter the Soul of the World.<br /> <br /> <b>Children of the Gods</b><br /> <br /> The Border Marches are a hunter's paradise, and that is no different for one of the Begotten. Like any other otherworld, they may take up Lair Chambers here, and the Hunting Bonus conferred by Pangaea itself makes a fine Lair Trait (Depths 1-2 being Minor and Depths 3-4 being Major). Beasts can open Primordial Pathways to the Border Marches just as they may open them to anywhere else, though this is generally unnecessary as you can effectively walk your way into the hunter's paradise if you intend to. The Hunting Bonus may be used normally, and confers its dice bonus to rolls to use Nightmares, but not the dice qualities (such as 9-again or rote action); dice qualities still benefit Atavisms.<br /> <br /> Ruins of the Time Before also make fascinating Lair Chambers, especially since a Beast is naturally immune to their Lair Traits. Being immune to Broken Time could render a Beast far more durable against the magics of the Sky-Wise, just as being able to call it down could make them a terrible scourge upon humanity.<br /> <br /> The Begotten have an interesting relationship to the Pangaeans, especially since fear of them birthed so many Horrors over time. Many of the Children have Horrors that may strongly resemble a given Pangaean god, and such Beasts often consider the god in question their 'parent' or at the very least a consort of the Dark Mother. It is extremely easy to pick up Chambers in the wake of a god's visit to the Flesh, or gain Satiety through invoking holy terror, taking advantage of a Horror resembling a god could lead to offending said god. Pangaeans are more than an equal to the Begotten, and the <i>last </i>thing a Beast wants is an offended deity storming into their Lair and tearing it apart.<br /> <br /> <b>The Broad Dreamers- Neolithic Heroes</b><br /> <br /> When the Dream was quiet and not filled with the chaos of millennia of myths and legends, Heroes were not affected by a constant stream of ideas telling them that their one and only duty was to calm the tempest within the Temenos by killing Beasts, they dreamed broad, but because of that they could read the passage of the Dream as surely as the Sky-Wise could account for the weather. A Hero was someone for the community to rally around, someone who could see the far-reaching view of the Primordial Dream and interpret the purpose of the nightmares. While the same things attracted the attention of Heroes, they knew better than to believe it was all about them. But should the Hero be unable to determine the lesson hidden within the nightmare, they still had a course of action left to them- seek out the Beast and ask them. The Hero was the <i>interpreter </i>of wisdom, but the Beast is the <i>keeper </i>of it, and while Heroes and Beasts would likely still never work together, their ideas on fear and its purpose very different, they could at the very least respect each other. The Beast knows fear in all its many flavours, they seek out their Kin to better understand it, and the Hero could depend on the Beast to know some obscure piece of lore that not even the Wise could uncover. Should all else fail, or a local Beast fall to the temptation of indulging its Hunger wantonly, the Hero could slay the Beast, becoming more powerful and more capable of defending their communities.<br /> <br /> Those Heroes who vainly believe that they are somehow better, those driven to obsessively hunt Beasts, still exist, but they are likely not accepted into the community the way that those Heroes who interpret nightmares are. These early precursors to Heracles, Beowulf, and others are often hunters and men of the woods- dangerous wandering travellers who are likely amongst the first to discover the arts of war.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-30T21:04:12-07:00","id":879232,"title":"","content":"Well, let me just start off by saying that I like the write-ups you made for Neolithic Beasts <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You did a good job in capturing the feel of the Begotten and Heroes of that time period. And just the thought of a Beast immune to the Broken Time Tilt is terrifying in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:58:50-07:00","id":880245,"title":"","content":"Thank-you. It most certainly is, especially considering that even just with the Advanced and Epic Iron Skin, or the Unbreakable Atavism, many Beasts would be effectively invincible to a Neolithic Hunter. Heroes and other supernatural beings would be pretty much the only things able to stand toe-to-toe with them. Here's some more stuff.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <b>One Big Screwed Up Family </b><br /> <br /> The Begotten don\u2019t yet identify themselves by Family, because they lack the mythic and folkloric framework to understand it. Most of the Children identify themselves as Kin based on the appearance of their Horrors, their Atavisms, and their Birthrights.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger Management </b><br /> <br /> A Beast in the Sundered World can effectively gorge themselves to their heart\u2019s content. Capable of Inflicting Nightmares whenever they desire, establishing Family Ties with Uratha goes a long way to being able to benefit from Family Dinner whenever they want. Following along with mortal hunters is of similar benefit. Simply skulking around the Border Marches for long enough gives them exceptional opportunity to witness hunts and feedings. As a result, the Begotten of this era are far more liberal with using Satiety, making them comparatively more dangerous.<br /> <br /> <b>Mother\u2019s Watching </b><br /> <br /> In the modern day, many of the Children have had a brush with the presence of the Dark Mother at least once in their lives. In the Sundered World, where gods walk astride the earth and the Dream is a still dark pool, she is even more present in the lives of her Children. She is a dark presence, far more vast and terrible than even the greatest of Horrors, she is a whispering voice calling them into the warm embrace of the Dream, she is love and acceptance like they\u2019ve never known, but she\u2019s also a nightmare to nightmares, a horror beyond anything. You can see her, sometimes, writhing just beneath the surface of the Dream- down where even Beasts fear to tread. She is Primal Fear, cold and eternal, fierce and ravenous even by the standards of Beasts. The Dark Mother can be merciless. Like Urfarah, the Firstborn, and the Pangaean gods, she occasionally involves herself with her Children in a visceral and tangible way- and the Begotten shudder in ecstasy and horror in remembrance of those fleeting occasions.<br /> <br /> <b>Inheritance</b><br /> <br /> All of the Inheritances are still present in the Sundered World, but it is worth acknowledging that in this time, where populations are smaller and more isolated and legends of mythic monsters spread like wildfire because the People are dead certain of the existence of monsters, that becoming a Beast Incarnate is much easier in this time. Some villages have a local Beast, and when that Child of the Dark Mother eventually spawns a Legend, they find themselves increasingly blessed by her power, capable of adopting the Beast-Shape.<br /> <br /> <b>Aftershocks</b><br /> <br /> When the Border Marches collapse into the Gauntlet, the effects are felt across the otherworlds. This last bastion of primal wilderness- a crossroads between Flesh, Shadow, Depths, and Dream -was what enabled the Horrors to roam freely. When the Gauntlet rises, Beasts find they are unable to maintain the form of their Horror outside their Lair. They cannot feed by Inflicting Nightmares. Their ability to manage their Hunger suffers a dramatic blow. Beasts who found themselves able to survive with a light touch and minimal suffering are driven to indulge their Hungers, suddenly plaguing communities they used to have at least cordial relationships with; some unable to live with their situation fall to the Merger. Heroes, left without other options, kill as many Beasts as they can, gathering up Gifts. Their Integrity suffers, and many become wandering monster hunters, killing every Begotten in their path. This chaotic time will eventually lead to the stories that clutter the Dream and taint future Heroes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T21:16:23-07:00","id":880724,"title":"","content":"So I don't think this has been asked, but what should we make of the Legacies of the Ancients in the context of the Neolithic? Some of them are definitely around while others may have cropped up later. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> DEMON, DEMON, DEMON! I can't believe we didn't think of this before. The Vinca have some of the earliest written language in the world. While it may have some elements of high speech, it likely has entirely mundane parts like it obviously does in real history. The Pact makers of this era are obvious... The potters. The People know the Wise exist, but they also probably don't know how they can impact people's day to day lives. Is a demon packing to bring someone good fortune going to be easily distinguishable from Fate magic? Not likely, unless you are Wise yourself. Potters are already associated with the Wise and magic, they already have the secrets of the written word! It is perfectly in cover for one of them to beseech the spirits on the behalf of the farmer to bring a good harvest. All the farmer has to do have to do is write their name in the side of a clay pot, which will then be fired so that they spirits know who's field to go to... Preferably in blood, so they can get your scent and come help even faster.<br /> <br /> Demons in the Vinca culture don't just work. They are such a tight fit that now I can't image the Sundered World without them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 05-03-2016, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T23:07:36-07:00","id":880761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=880724#post880724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't think this has been asked, but what should we make of the Legacies of the Ancients in the context of the Neolithic? Some of them are definitely around while others may have cropped up later. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally I wouldn't use any of them. Even the Dreamspeakers wouldn't make sense in context of the much more imminent Pangeans. And personally I don't buy the rhetoric about the primal non-Atlantean Elemental Tamers. They're clearly based on the shared Greco-Indian model of the five elements, not universal rooted human concepts you find in the Neolithic Cosmology (note the different associations of the Paths compared to the &quot;To the Strongest&quot; associations matching the Tamers).<br /> <br /> For the People I'm working on<br /> <br /> - Hollow Keepers (Forest-Wise, Potters &amp; Realm Sojourners; Death primary)<br /> - Wind-Singers (Sky-Wise, harmonious warders; Spirit primary)<br /> - Bull's Children (Storm-Wise Wealthy Chiefs; Fate primary)<br /> - Bird's Children (Sky-Wise Oracles; Prime primary)<br /> - Snake's Children (Water-Wise Healers; Life primary)<br /> - Wolf's Children (Blood-Wise Hunters; Space primary)<br /> - Flame Fathers/Mothers (Storm-Wise Coppersmiths, Matter primary)<br /> <br /> - Shattered (proto Left-Handed explorers of Shattered Time; Time primary)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:21:34-07:00","id":880887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=880724#post880724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I don't think this has been asked, but what should we make of the Legacies of the Ancients in the context of the Neolithic? Some of them are definitely around while others may have cropped up later. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> DEMON, DEMON, DEMON! I can't believe we didn't think of this before. The Vinca have some of the earliest written language in the world. While it may have some elements of high speech, it likely has entirely mundane parts like it obviously does in real history. The Pact makers of this era are obvious... The potters. The People know the Wise exist, but they also probably don't know how they can impact people's day to day lives. Is a demon packing to bring someone good fortune going to be easily distinguishable from Fate magic? Not likely, unless you are Wise yourself. Potters are already associated with the Wise and magic, they already have the secrets of the written word! It is perfectly in cover for one of them to beseech the spirits on the behalf of the farmer to bring a good harvest. All the farmer has to do have to do is write their name in the side of a clay pot, which will then be fired so that they spirits know who's field to go to... Preferably in blood, so they can get your scent and come help even faster.<br /> <br /> Demons in the Vinca culture don't just work. They are such a tight fit that now I can't image the Sundered World without them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very curious to see how a write-up of the Unchained in the Sundered World would turn out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:39:09-07:00","id":880895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=880887#post880887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very curious to see how a write-up of the Unchained in the Sundered World would turn out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm on it. I'm busy with work, so it may take a few weeks, but I'm on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:05:44-07:00","id":881465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=880761#post880761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Personally I wouldn't use any of them. Even the Dreamspeakers wouldn't make sense in context of the much more imminent Pangeans. And personally I don't buy the rhetoric about the primal non-Atlantean Elemental Tamers. They're clearly based on the shared Greco-Indian model of the five elements, not universal rooted human concepts you find in the Neolithic Cosmology (note the different associations of the Paths compared to the &quot;To the Strongest&quot; associations matching the Tamers).<br /> <br /> For the People I'm working on<br /> <br /> - Hollow Keepers (Forest-Wise, Potters &amp; Realm Sojourners; Death primary)<br /> - Wind-Singers (Sky-Wise, harmonious warders; Spirit primary)<br /> - Bull's Children (Storm-Wise Wealthy Chiefs; Fate primary)<br /> - Bird's Children (Sky-Wise Oracles; Prime primary)<br /> - Snake's Children (Water-Wise Healers; Life primary)<br /> - Wolf's Children (Blood-Wise Hunters; Space primary)<br /> - Flame Fathers/Mothers (Storm-Wise Coppersmiths, Matter primary)<br /> <br /> - Shattered (proto Left-Handed explorers of Shattered Time; Time primary)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, idea on another one, less developed than the others. They'd be Water-Wise who serve as &quot;memory&quot; of the community, expanding their consciouness to take on the memories, stories, and even personalities of the dead - sort of benevolent Reapers. Would that work as a Mind favored Legacy, or do you think it would have to be Death?<br /> <br /> As I know people's preference, I'm leaning away from Legacies whose primary Arcana is one the Path already favors, and instead using those as secondary Arcana; like Bird's Children use Prime for &quot;revelation/truth-speaking&quot; while their Time or Fate ratings open up their soothsaying effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:12:28-07:00","id":881471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=881465#post881465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, idea on another one, less developed than the others. They'd be Water-Wise who serve as &quot;memory&quot; of the community, expanding their consciouness to take on the memories, stories, and even personalities of the dead - sort of benevolent Reapers. Would that work as a Mind favored Legacy, or do you think it would have to be Death?<br /> <br /> As I know people's preference, I'm leaning away from Legacies whose primary Arcana is one the Path already favors, and instead using those as secondary Arcana; like Bird's Children use Prime for &quot;revelation/truth-speaking&quot; while their Time or Fate ratings open up their soothsaying effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Mind would be the Legacy's Primary Arcanum, with Death allowing for them to recover the memories of the recently deceased as well as restoring the memories of ghosts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T01:56:01-07:00","id":884474,"title":"","content":"Idle thought regarding Sundered World Demons. Does anyone have ideas on how to weave in the God-Machine flavor text in the CoFD core and the Giants in the Earth shard from the Demon Storytellers' Guide together with this particular Dark Era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T16:38:43-07:00","id":885000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=884474#post884474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idle thought regarding Sundered World Demons. Does anyone have ideas on how to weave in the God-Machine flavor text in the CoFD core and the Giants in the Earth shard from the Demon Storytellers' Guide together with this particular Dark Era?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm working on it. I have and entire cosmology that evolves from the way Voice of the Angel is described and it is very likely to creep back into my write up, so I won't spoil it yet. I need to read Giants in the Earth again, but I do want to include the Nephiliem in my write up, so I'm likely going to take some inspiration from that shard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:05:04-07:00","id":885675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=880761#post880761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I wouldn't use any of them. Even the Dreamspeakers wouldn't make sense in context of the much more imminent Pangeans. And personally I don't buy the rhetoric about the primal non-Atlantean Elemental Tamers. They're clearly based on the shared Greco-Indian model of the five elements, not universal rooted human concepts you find in the Neolithic Cosmology (note the different associations of the Paths compared to the &quot;To the Strongest&quot; associations matching the Tamers).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree at all from a real-life historical perspective, but it seems pretty clear that the world Before the Fall was quite a bit different - quite aside from the fact that it was far more magically active, there's even different versions of history that are likely completely valid because, after all, Time and Fate are Arcana, too. We're told that the very continents <i>might</i> have been different, with the Daksha claiming that a place called Lemuria preceeded the so-called Atlantis and more.<br /> <br /> If anything, one could argue that the Greeks &quot;rediscovered&quot; the pre-Fall mode of thinking after it had become muddled over time. Ignoring the existing lore on the Tamers strikes me as a bit much, just because it doesn't fit into the modern scholarship about that period doesn't mean it shouldn't be valid within the context of the &quot;actual&quot; history of the gameline's world. You could even get modern scholars scoffing at such a concept, and a Time-lost mage from our time popping back and being stunned at the strangeness she sees that just didn't make it into the archaeological record, because the Sleeping Curse has swallowed up many of these Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 04-28-2017, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:10:22-07:00","id":885685,"title":"","content":"Ok, but if you want to go with a rediscovery in the Hellenistic Era of something from the Time Before, that still doesn't put them in the Neolithic Era, where the Paths have different &quot;elemental&quot; associations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:34:53-07:00","id":886680,"title":"","content":"Anyone working on Sundered innocents? and does anyone know if there's a community 2e rule conversion for innocents?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T02:08:37-07:00","id":887051,"title":"","content":"Damn it. I need one more Legacy and I will have 2 for each Path, favoring all 10 Arcana. Any ideas for a Time favoring Forest-Wise Legacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T05:16:45-07:00","id":887087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=887051#post887051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn it. I need one more Legacy and I will have 2 for each Path, favoring all 10 Arcana. Any ideas for a Time favoring Forest-Wise Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps one that deals with navigation somehow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T05:35:00-07:00","id":887093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=887051#post887051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn it. I need one more Legacy and I will have 2 for each Path, favoring all 10 Arcana. Any ideas for a Time favoring Forest-Wise Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bA Legacy attempting to look into the *future* version of the Astral, hoping to find new secrets and knowledge which haven't even happened yet (but theoretically might) that can be exploited for the People?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:41:20-07:00","id":887150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=887093#post887093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bA Legacy attempting to look into the *future* version of the Astral, hoping to find new secrets and knowledge which haven't even happened yet (but theoretically might) that can be exploited for the People?</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, that's a good idea, they'd make a fantastic modern day one as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T08:15:44-07:00","id":887181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=887150#post887150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, that's a good idea, they'd make a fantastic modern day one as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded.<br /> <br /> Say, what do people think about making the modern name of that Legacy something along the lines of Astropath? (yes, taken straight from Warhammer 40K)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:22:07-07:00","id":887278,"title":"","content":"Astropath pretty much means 'star suffering' so would be an odd choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:40:40-07:00","id":887289,"title":"","content":"I definitely love the concept in the modern setting. I'm not sure the People have enough of a sense of chronological advancement for it to make thematic sense for them though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:42:34-07:00","id":887292,"title":"","content":"I have a time-based proto-Left-handed Legacy (trying to spread shattered time to reclaim the Time Before). I could just make them Forest-Wise Primary (currently they're not tied to any Path).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T04:59:16-07:00","id":888066,"title":"","content":"Story hook for a Mage game inspired by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/855280-pangaea-unleashed?p=888055#post888055\">this little drabble of mine</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 </b>Panic has broken out among the Wise as several of their Circles find themselves falling prey to magic beyond the abilities of any among their number. Matters only worsen when they realize that the spells are being channeled through a number of Omphalos Stones, those bestowed upon them by Bird and Bull. Have the two Pangaeans finally had enough of their hunts for the hearts of their fellow gods? Or are they enacting retribution for one Circle's attempts to seize the remainder of their power? Whatever the reasons, the Wise must scramble to work together to stop these attacks before their villages fall to the very power that was meant to protect them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:40:18-07:00","id":888124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=880724#post880724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DEMON, DEMON, DEMON! I can't believe we didn't think of this before. The Vinca have some of the earliest written language in the world. While it may have some elements of high speech, it likely has entirely mundane parts like it obviously does in real history. The Pact makers of this era are obvious... The potters. The People know the Wise exist, but they also probably don't know how they can impact people's day to day lives. Is a demon packing to bring someone good fortune going to be easily distinguishable from Fate magic? Not likely, unless you are Wise yourself. Potters are already associated with the Wise and magic, they already have the secrets of the written word! It is perfectly in cover for one of them to beseech the spirits on the behalf of the farmer to bring a good harvest. All the farmer has to do have to do is write their name in the side of a clay pot, which will then be fired so that they spirits know who's field to go to... Preferably in blood, so they can get your scent and come help even faster.<br /> <br /> Demons in the Vinca culture don't just work. They are such a tight fit that now I can't image the Sundered World without them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another significant reason behind potters being advantageous Covers for the Unchained, and that's likely because the potters are significant to the God-Machine's projects as well. The potters wield god-words and turn them into ritual ceramics, but what would happen if a Messenger whispered in their ear, changing the god-words? What would happen should a Psychopomp influence a village to be planned out <i>just so</i>, with altered ritual ceramics buried under the homes making some of the first occult matrixes? In a village without the Wise, the elders lift up a great menhir carved in symbols that the Wise don't even recognize, words of a distant, alien god.<br /> <br /> Imagine potters and coppersmiths working together, forming hollow statues of clay, metal, and the ashes of sacrifices, an Angel filling it as it hardens in a kiln. Imagine Angels using Incepts freely, without fear, for the Unchained are rare and the God-Machine's projects must be swiftly protected with overwhelming force and completed with impossible speed and scale to gain a foothold in a world of wild gods. It's predictive algorithms know the Sundering is close at hand, and when it comes its First Legion will emerge from the shadows, building things unlike anything that has ever been seen before. It will subvert the humans, and make them its willing servants for its own inscrutable purposes.<br /> <br /> I imagine the bodies of these Angels to strongly resemble the void-ash armour of the angels in Kill Six Billion Demons.<br /> <br /> As a side note, it is also worth mentioning that the crossover section calls out potters as the main source of Prometheans that aren't just naturally occurring Extemporae, so you have the potters working with the Wise, fending off spirits, and being whispered to by angels of molten metal and living flame. Very busy guys, those Vinca potters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T17:07:50-07:00","id":888666,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> <br /> <br /> You just put up the first tidbits for a full-on Sundered World Demon write-up, dude. Great job. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I browsed for pictures on those Angels you mentioned, and I think I can second your thoughts on that as well. Plus, is it just me or would some of those Vinca potters function similarly to Alchemists? We might have to wait a little for the Promethean 2E pdf to come out, but still...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T22:13:08-07:00","id":888840,"title":"","content":"With &quot;the Pack&quot; now out, I need to pick Sacred Hunts for the faction-based Lodges I'm going to write-up.<br /> <br /> The Loyal: Those Who Violate Father Wolf's Law<br /> <br /> The Cull: Humanity<br /> <br /> The Maw: Werewolves<br /> <br /> The Shepherds: Predators that Prey on Humanity<br /> <br /> The Inheritors: ???<br /> <br /> The Devourers: Father Wolf &amp; Loyal Firstborn<br /> <br /> The Mourners: ???<br /> <br /> Tyrants: ???<br /> <br /> <br /> To be clear, the factions are much larger than Lodges, but their privileges to those who have distinguished themselves as represented through the lodge mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T02:30:57-07:00","id":888975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=888840#post888840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With &quot;the Pack&quot; now out, I need to pick Sacred Hunts for the faction-based Lodges I'm going to write-up.<br /> <br /> To be clear, the factions are much larger than Lodges, but their privileges to those who have distinguished themselves as represented through the lodge mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>When they do get posted, you mind if I tweak them for use in Age of Azar, seeing as the time difference between it and the Sundered World is still only a few thousand years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T08:38:02-07:00","id":889145,"title":"","content":"I'm having difficulty visualizing the interaction between the world of Flesh, Spirit, and the Border Marches. I assumed it was like a sort of overlap - venn diagram style - but I don't think that's quite right.<br /> <br /> On one hand a Depth rating of 5 is represents you're really deep in the Marches; you're kind of cut off from the Flesh and the Spirit. But Depth 1 acts as like a locus so that it's basically just a thin, short walk into the Shadow? So it's not like an overlap in my mind; I see it more as like a circle that's thick in the center and thins outward, but this circle is everywhere, right? The Border Marches are the whole of nature and the world except for where the People build?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T14:15:02-07:00","id":889351,"title":"","content":"I think a Venn diagram is actually an spot on representation. Notice that you can cross trough the middle of the intersection and it takes more than to cross through one of the borders. Is sorta like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:18:56-07:00","id":889427,"title":"","content":"Is there any mundane wilderness, though, or is the whole world basically the Marches?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:48:26-07:00","id":889460,"title":"","content":"The non-intersection area of one of the circles is mundane wilderness, that in the Flesh. There's also spiritual wilderness in the Shadow, reflecting the physical one, as usual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T17:43:39-07:00","id":889504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=889427#post889427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any mundane wilderness, though, or is the whole world basically the Marches?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the world is mostly &quot;mundane&quot; and that to get to the Marches you either have to know where you're going, or be very far off the beaten path indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T18:47:58-07:00","id":889535,"title":"","content":"Reseru, am i correct that what's either surprising or confusing you is that it's areas that are very spiritual (a hollow for example) where depth is small, making it seem like in your model there isn't much overlap - but areas where the flesh and the shadow are far from each other, there is a great deal of Pangea, meaning there's a lot of overlap?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T20:07:18-07:00","id":889582,"title":"","content":"Yeah, basically. The way it seems is that in a region of mundane wilderness the Depth rating would be 0, but Depth 1 basically acts as a locus already.<br /> <br /> Like...the Marches are still another 'plane' right? It just overlaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T20:30:45-07:00","id":889594,"title":"","content":"Depth 1 are Loci, if memory doesn't deceive me. A region in the mundane Wilderness means more symbolic resonance with the Border Marches, so they have greater Depth. The wilder, the better. The Uratha like the shallows because that's where it's most likely things of the Flesh or Shadow will attempt to cross over because it's a short walk, a matter of seconds or minutes, and that's really tempting for a Spirit or one of the Wise.<br /> <br /> The Depths offer greater benefits to hunting, but it can take weeks to cross them and gods live in there, making them far more dangerous. You can just walk into and out of them though- Wits + Survival I think. Fail a regular navigation roll and you can stumble into Pangaea by accident. Because transition is easier, you also need to make rolls to avoid running into any Spirits that are hanging around the Flesh.<br /> <br /> I'll hopefully have something else for Sundered World Demons tomorrow. A little more elaboration on what the God-Machine's doing, what Angels are doing and how they're different, what Demons do in society and how they handle it, though I get the feeling it would be more productive just to read the Aztec chapter to get ideas towards that end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T03:46:58-07:00","id":889778,"title":"","content":"Now...I understand that a dramatic failure in the wild can put you on a path to the Marches. Let me ask this, though: without a Gauntlet, and if there's no Marches in the area, does that mean that the whole world is a Verge for the Shadow basically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T07:50:58-07:00","id":889888,"title":"","content":"Not quite. The Gauntlet <i>is </i>the Border Marches, crushed into some kind of massive scab or scar across the entire world, and the reason the Gauntlet is thickest around human inhabitation is because it has the least Resonance with Pangaea, which despite being a whole other realm was also the primary means of going back and forth between the worlds. In the Sundered World, where humans build there are no Marches, and because there are no Marches there's no way to cross over from Flesh to Shadow- the route is completely blocked.<br /> <br /> This eventually transitions into the modern status quo. Human building = Basically impossible to cross. Wild Places = Easy transition due to Resonance with Pangaea. Loci = As always, quick crossing points between worlds. In the Sundered World, a Locus is even more dramatic than normal. There's no need to Reach, no need to perform some sort of ritual to gain access, you can simply walk into a Locus, spend thirty seconds walking through the Marches, and end up in the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:14:28-07:00","id":897936,"title":"","content":"Well this has been a long time coming, but I <i>really </i>wanted to get this right. Hopefully everyone likes it. Ladies and gentlemen, the Unchained of the Sundered World.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <b>Sundered World Demons</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Machine</i>: There is more than one god wandering the world before the Sundering, and that means the God-Machine needs to work with an extraordinarily light touch. Pangaeans are more than a match for all but the most powerful of its Angels, the <i>Diharim</i> howl from the Hisil, the High Chieftains of Faerie and the first Gods of the Thistle can walk the world freely before it becomes Ironside, and in the lands that will be called Kemet the temakh still serve Azar. Even long after Irem vanished from the world, the Machine will order Its servants to avoid the ruins and relics.<br /> <br /> Areas of Infrastructure are as devoid of the presence of the Border Marches as anything constructed by man, Facilities can be confused with Ruins of the Time Before, and time splinters are mistaken for Emanation Realms. It is in these places, where the Machine can be sure It is alone, that It manifests in all Its power. The few Angels that exist spend most of their time in Facilities and time splinters, but some are still sent forth in order to perform Missions and oversee Infrastructure. These Angels are different than the ones that come later, a little more self-aware, a little more creative, given full license to use their Incepts whenever and however they see fit in order to be able to effectively defend themselves against the other creatures that may be watching over or using a given village.<br /> <br /> The works of the God-Machine don\u2019t reveal themselves quite as much in clockworks and oil, but in ceramics and stone. A village is arranged just so, ceramics with the words of a distant deity are buried under homes instead of the god-words of the Wise, a menhir carved with strange symbols, rivers and forests shaped with extremely specific earthworks to produce occult matrixes of their own, fires that refuse to burn out. An Angel could bend an entire village to its will, using them to mine gold and copper to produce circuitry for the God-Machine\u2019s more complex projects. The bodies of Angels come in many forms, in pottery and statuary and copper ornamentation, in sacrificed humans and animals, in obsidian and wood.<br /> <br /> The most common of the God-Machine\u2019s servants in these days are Imperatives, flocks of them will descend upon a village It intends to subvert, often leaving the local Wise baffled. Imperatives are simple Ephemera, too simple to even be touched by any of the Arcana, and make excellent Mysteries. However, they are virtually impossible to halt or command without outright destroying them. Many Wise, apart from the Blood-Wise who are most familiar with the Shadow, will probably dismiss them as an irritating but relatively harmless spiritual phenomenon.<br /> <br /> <i>The Outcasts</i><b>:</b> The Unchained are rare, but not unheard of, and in a world where the God-Machine isn\u2019t nearly as omnipresent their numbers start to accumulate over time. They are all drawn to Infrastructure, both as insight into their Ciphers and as one of the only sources of Aether they can find. Fortunately for most of the outcasts, Infrastructure is often close at hand, and it is usually the Infrastructure they established themselves. Where the Unchained do walk, they have a tendency to either hide or rule. It is a smaller world, with tighter communities, and becoming trusted enough to start making Pacts or gain a Cover that could enable them to live a relatively eccentric life is a difficult thing. Among the most common Covers that demons seek out are traders. Because the People, like many cultures of the time, have trade based on gift giving, Pacts are easily concealed as business deals. As a result, Patchwork Covers are common, with demons arriving from the wilds as a lost, but familiar, stranger.<br /> <br /> The generous trader wanders their route, giving gifts of pottery with strange symbols, or textiles with unusual weaves, and asks for nothing in return but abstractions- relationships, memories, misfortunes -while heaping blessings on the heads of those who take them up. How could they say no, when their work is so obviously lucky? How could they say no, when they expects so little in return? Everyone loves the trader.<br /> <br /> The hunter disappears for long stretches of time, alone, as is their custom. Everyone thinks they\u2019re mad, but they always seem to come back. They are a master of beasts, served by strange monsters that can only come from the Border Marches, marked by peculiar scars, and changed by their visits to places of the Time Before. They might be feared, but they\u2019re also respected. When they say a terrible spirit is coming to end their way of life, they are believed, and a hunting party heads out with them. Many often return with the same odd scars and unbelievable stories. They rarely speak of what they have seen, and spend more and more time with the hunter.<br /> <br /> The elder will not be moved, and no shaman or Wise One will dissuade them from changing some aspect of the traditions. These ceramics should be buried <i>here</i> instead of <i>there</i>, they should be marked with these new signs, that earthwork should be torn down and a new one built here, we should honor the gods with these sacrifices instead. No one understands how they get away with it all, but they are just so <i>persuasive</i>.<br /> <br /> The potter is a strange one, living on the outskirts of the village in a hut that has been blasted by lightning and scorched by flame. They have no Wise One, so the potter makes due as their shaman. The ceramics they make resemble nothing the People have ever seen, but they <i>must</i> work, because gifts of them have pleased the local spirits. The power this potter puts into the ceramics is like nothing the Wise have ever seen, for it does not trigger the Sleeping Curse and anyone can wield them. Their village is well armed against what is in the dark, but the potter doesn\u2019t cease making increasingly elaborate and powerful works of art and some fear they know something\u2019s coming and aren\u2019t willing to speak of it.<br /> <br /> <i>Those Who Can See</i><b>:</b> Stigmatics are, understandably, a little rarer in these days. But where they appear, they appear in force. Whole villages are co-opted by the God-Machine for a project, and the inhabitants either become active parts of the project, or are warped by the proximity to active Infrastructure. They are not ember-bearers as understood by the Wise, and a god, but not one that the People normally worship has touched them. Villages of Stigmatics are peculiarities and terrors to the rest of the People, with strange traditions and frightful marks, they are mad oracles marching to the beat of an eldritch drum, following the path of a wheel even the Sky-Wise can\u2019t see. These settlements are actively avoided, but in time a Circle of the Wise will be called to go and investigate. When they arrive, likely expecting a discrete being to appease, they find instead nothing to placate and only an otherworldly herald, an Angel, one of the God-Machine\u2019s hands and feet. It is the Storm-Wise who are most likely to grasp what the God-Machine is, not a being but a force, something that moves and is moved in turn.<br /> <br /> In a village that has a resident Unchained, however, the situation is often rather different. The demon recognizes others who are touched by the same hands that made it, and sees in them potential allies that can be told just enough to be made dangerous to their enemy. Those Stigmatics blessed with an Unchained patron find belonging and community of a human sort, and not the clockwork harmony of the Machine\u2019s order, often organizing into a sort of cult around the demon. They tame cryptids and battle Angels; they make deals with their patron for power, and take up fantastical works of pottery that function as the hardware for the first Gadgets. One demon may slowly gather up enough Pacts to make a Patchwork Cover or several, preparing lives for decades and even centuries to come.<br /> <br /> The small god embodied in a demon surrounds itself with children who resemble its form of perfection, and they\u2019re groomed to attain desirable aspects to become the next incarnation of the village\u2019s god. Some may only settle by taking tribute in the form of Pacts for desirable qualities of these children who will be heavily compensated. Others may become so enamored with a particular life that they want it all for themselves.<br /> <br /> The cult of Stigmatics surrounding a demon beat down low-Rank Exiles, caging them with Bans and Banes. In time their patron will ascend, regaining its immortality and some of the raw might of its angelic Incarnation. Perhaps it will even find a way to become one with the Infrastructure it subverted, becoming a small God-Machine in its own right.<br /> <br /> <i>Wonders and Horrors</i><b>:</b> For the most part hidden from the God-Machine\u2019s gaze by virtue of distance and Its need for concealment, the Unchained have a little more freedom to act. They can walk about in their true form and wield Exploits, but their greatest works remain the construction of powerful Gadgets. Most use ceramics, as unusual, magically potent, pieces of pottery are common amongst the Vinca. Others will raid Infrastructure for rare iron and gold, while others will use the ornamental, but readily available, copper. Gadgets installed into Pacts are more common in these days, when a Pact is liable to be a worked stone or a piece of pottery, and a village supported by a prolific Unchained Gadget-maker is in some ways more powerful than one supported by the Wise. Many Gadgets can be wielded by anyone, and a Gadget can be in anything suitably symbolically resonant. Perhaps the carved menhir symbolizing the villagers\u2019 oaths to their Unchained patron is a Gadget a dozen times over, with different effects installed into each individual Pact, making it an unspeakably powerful Lambda. Perhaps a grove of sacred trees protects the village, or lidded pots can become traps for spirits.<br /> <br /> The Demon-Blooded are more common in these days as well, especially since in a tight-knit community relationships are a little more expected. At a distance from the God-Machine, they can more freely communicate with their parents, and many grow up proud of their natural capabilities and what they can do. The most powerful of all the Demon-Blooded are the Nephilim, an unexpected consequence of the Unchained condition the God-Machine will later produce Infrastructure to rectify. When a Demon-Blooded is born, roll their parent\u2019s Primum. If they are a Fractal, roll the <i>lower</i> of their parents\u2019 Primum. If any successes result, they become a Nephil, with all the benefits and drawbacks that entails. This <i>can</i> stack with the traits of ordinary Demon-Blooded, so you can be a Nephil Offspring, or a Nephil Fractal. A Fractal who joins the ranks of the Nephilim is likely the closest thing to a natural-born demon that exists in the world, and in some ways they are something\u2026 more. Able to overclock Embeds and even determine when one of the Unchained is lying, capable of wielding the power of Exploits and transform into a Demonic Form of their own, a Nephil Fractal is an unholy terror, a demigod astride the earth.<br /> <br /> <i>The Cipher</i><b>:</b> For the Unchained, the Cipher is an answer, a puzzle, a mystery, a pilgrimage, and possibly a trap. For the Demon-Blooded, it is a chain they wrap around themselves. Unexpected result of the Fall or not, the Demon-Blooded are of the Machine, and their power stems from it. If the Unchained Cipher is something unexpected that draws them <i>away</i> from the Machine, then the Demon-Blooded Cipher is something unexpected that draws them <i>to </i>the Machine. The Nephilim possess unstable souls, the crackling core of Primum within them liable to shred their sense of identity. However, they <i>can</i> stem the effects of their Unstable soul\u2026 by choosing to spend a point of Willpower and suffer a Compromise instead. This functions as per <b>Flowers of Hell</b>, advancing their Cipher.<br /> <br /> Some Unchained, early Pentagramists, are unhappy with a limit to their power, and some even see the Cipher as another limitation imposed by their creator. They force a fifth Key into their Cipher, breaking it, reforming it, potentially discovering true freedom and becoming utterly unchained. While the mysteries of the Cipher make the beliefs of Pentagramists mysterious and dubious at best, the Pentagram is the salvation of the Demon-Blooded. In forcing in a fifth Key, they shatter their Cipher, and in doing so shatter the God-Machine\u2019s hold on them. Forcing the Pentagram immediately forces a Breaking Point with a -5 penalty; with all the risks it holds for the Unchained. For Offspring, the burden is relatively light- a single point of Aggravated damage and a permanent catastrophic glitch. For the Nephilim, it is far riskier, and potentially fatal in more ways than one as it tears at the flesh and the soul alike. But if they survive the procedure, they find themselves freed. The Activated Condition resolves, and they no longer suffer the modified Demon-Blooded form of Compromise, instead using the Unchained version (minus the loss of Cover).<br /> <br /> A Pentagramist Demon-Blooded is a free agent in the Sundered World- unique, unspeakably powerful, and a possible origin for myths of demons, angels, gods, and demigods. They are truly the great men of old, heroes of renown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T11:41:04-07:00","id":898028,"title":"","content":"Especially loving the out for the Demon-Blooded Pentagramists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T16:49:57-07:00","id":898384,"title":"","content":"Are &quot;Imperatives&quot; mentioned elsewhere? curious about them. Also how would you suggest dealing with compromise? if Demons can to some extent walk in their true form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 05-24-2016, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T17:04:53-07:00","id":898402,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=898384#post898384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are &quot;Imperatives&quot; mentioned elsewhere? curious about them. Also how would you suggest dealing with compromise? if Demons can to some extent walk in their true form.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're mentioned in the Demon Storytellers' Guide. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\">Minor servants of the God-Machine not sophisticated enough to be called angels&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> Moving on. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>, you did a really good job presenting a write-up for Demons in the Sundered World. Not to mention weave in the Nephilim from DStG into the mix. Regarding the Nephilim, though, I'd probably make them a separate type of Demon-Blooded instead of being a sub-category of Offspring and/or Fractal. But that's just my own preference.<br /> <br /> I'm also liking the idea behind the Pentagram as well. Giving Demon-Blooded a potential out from the God-Machine's influence is a really interesting concept.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-24-2016, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T17:14:40-07:00","id":898416,"title":"","content":"Awesome job! I'm glad that while I've been crunched for time and unable to write up my version of the Unchained in the Sundered World, our visions at least ran parallel to one another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T20:12:30-07:00","id":901678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=898402#post898402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Moving on. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>, you did a really good job presenting a write-up for Demons in the Sundered World. Not to mention weave in the Nephilim from DStG into the mix. Regarding the Nephilim, though, I'd probably make them a separate type of Demon-Blooded instead of being a sub-category of Offspring and/or Fractal. But that's just my own preference.<br /> <br /> I'm also liking the idea behind the Pentagram as well. Giving Demon-Blooded a potential out from the God-Machine's influence is a really interesting concept.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Looking back, I <i>think</i> making them a separate type of Demon-Blooded would probably be wiser, but I like the idea of Fractal Nephilim, if only due to the fact that they're basically flesh-and-blood, natural-born, Unchained. Tying in the Pentagram (which I can't take credit for, it's a hack from the DStG) to the Demon-Blooded just seemed natural to me. The belief that the Cipher is a controlling influence from the God-Machine is just conjecture for the Unchained, but it is reality for the Demon-Blooded, and I liked the idea that what is- possibly -a trap for one might be the salvation of the other. The Pentagram freeing the Demon-Blooded just feels... right, somehow. Like it's a satisfying ending to the story.<br /> <br /> I also just loved the idea of the Pentagram for its extremely Gnostic attitude. Even if you're free of the God-Machine/Demiurge, even if you've expanded your Primum and completed your Cipher and truly anchored yourself in the world and established your Hell away from It, you still are <i>of </i>It, and the Cipher is still a relic of Its design. How does one become truly free then? In kabbalah, crossing the gap between the lower seven sephiroth and up to the Supernal Triad is referred to as &quot;crossing the Abyss&quot;. When it's a qlippthotic, or Left-Hand process, &quot;crossing the Abyss&quot; is still a test, but the end result isn't union with the divine, but total separation from it and establishing yourself on top. Utter separation, utter freedom- the true definition of Hell, a place away from God.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> EDIT: As a side note, I'm trying to think of ways to mechanically handle Changelings, the Hedge, Huntsmen, and True Fae in the Sundered World. Any suggestions? I know <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> had a lot of stuff they were suggesting for Changeling and what the Changeling narrative is at this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T07:07:35-07:00","id":902023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=901678#post901678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back, I <i>think</i> making them a separate type of Demon-Blooded would probably be wiser, but I like the idea of Fractal Nephilim, if only due to the fact that they're basically flesh-and-blood, natural-born, Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>To each his own, I suppose. But I'm still leaning more for Nephilim as a separate type. Seeing as in the StG, they <i>don't</i> have Interlocks, Keys, and Ciphers. Will probably take a stab at it when the internet isn't as crappy as it is, right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=901678#post901678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: As a side note, I'm trying to think of ways to mechanically handle Changelings, the Hedge, Huntsmen, and True Fae in the Sundered World. Any suggestions? I know <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> had a lot of stuff they were suggesting for Changeling and what the Changeling narrative is at this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing on mechanics. But expect me to work out some fluff for Neolithic Lost. Specifically how they live among (or apart from) the rest of the People.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 05-28-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:44:46-07:00","id":902745,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any thoughts about handling Supernal Entities in a Neolithic setting? I got some notes being written down on the subject, but I am curious to hear how their systems could be tweaked to fit with the era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T10:35:59-07:00","id":902801,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Supernal Entities in the Sundered World</u></b><br /> <br /> The Wise believe that the Pangaeans are fallen gods, former inhabitants of the Supernal World. When the Time Before came crashing down to its end, these divine beings were forever sundered from the realms they called home. But there were other gods who did not suffer this fate, entities who tied themselves so deeply with their domains that they cannot stray from them without risking their destruction. Particularly experienced Wise can learn and perform ceremonies which call these deities forth for a time, but some have been known to manifest on their own in the World of Flesh through sacred places not unlike the Border Marches. Regardless of how they appear, though, the appearance of such beings is considered an auspicious omen by the People.<br /> <br /> Beings native to the Supernal World are more powerful in this era than they are in succeeding millennia. Part of this stems from the wilder and more fiery nature of the realms at the time. But the state of the world before the Sundering is another reason why they thrive as they do.<br /> <br /> In this world, magic is abundant and a part of everyday reality. The Sleeping Curse is not as pervasive an influence among mortals as it will be in modern nights, and many remnants from the Time Before have yet to erode from centuries of Dissonance. All this makes it possible for Supernal Entities to exist a little longer, but they must still return to their home realms, lest they be dragged into the depths of the Outside.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the rules for Supernal Entities remain the same. However, they are able to exist in the Fallen World for longer stretches of time due to the world having more tentative ties to the Supernal World. A Supernal being summoned by one of the Wise suffers a point of Corpus damage for each <i>day</i> that it stays in the circle. If it leaves the circle, it suffers this damage every twelve hours. And if it comes into contact with Sleepers, this time interval is further reduced to six hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The End of an Era</b><br /> <br /> The death of the Great Predator, and the subsequent rise of the Gauntlet created ripples that extended all the way to the Supernal World. And just as the Wise have their influence wane in the aftermath, so too do Supernal Entities find their ability to spend time in the Fallen World lessen. Dissonance eventually erases the scars of the Time Before, and the Pangaeans gradually shed their knowledge of the Arcana in order to cope in the changed world. With fewer tethers to the Supernal Realms, the World of Flesh becomes increasingly more corrosive to these otherwise powerful gods. The Awakened who continue to summon them for guidance now do so sparingly, as few are loathe to cause the death of such a being by trapping it in the Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T06:19:08-07:00","id":908288,"title":"","content":"Would appreciate help in developing this :3 <hr /><br /> <b><u>Turtle, Calm and Contemplative</u></b><br /> Though an unfamiliar god to most of the Vinca, this Pangaean is honored by coastal and seafaring tribes in different parts of the world. He is also one of the very few denizens of the Border Marches who can pass into the Worlds of Spirit and Flesh without facing reprisal from Urfarah. Uratha and Wise Ones who know of this often wonder why this is so. Some say that the Turtle is a being equal to the Great Predator in age and power. Others think the Pangaean simply earned it by besting Wolf in a confrontation. Whatever the reason, Turtle could move freely between the worlds, and uses this privilege to gather knowledge wherever he went.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T08:16:56-07:00","id":908343,"title":"","content":"To answer the question of what Compromise looks like for the Unchained in the Sundered World, you could always use the rules for the Exclusion Zone on pg. 114 of the Demon Storyteller's Guide. Mechanically, it adds +3 to all Compromises and the Unchained don't have to roll for Compromise for remaining in Demonic Form for more than one scene.<br /> <br /> In regards to Turtle, Calm and Contemplative, a good place to start would probably be Demantu the Abyssal Queen, a powerful Lune in War Against the Pure on pg. 127 It is worth noting that beyond being symbols of wisdom and longevity, turtle symbolism actually has a rather vicious dark side. In Nigeria the turtle is a trickster, the most cunning of all animals. In Ancient Egypt it was called &quot;an abomination to Ra&quot; and killed as an evil creature. It is associated with the Underworld in Ancient Egypt and in other cultures, and a leaf cut to resemble a turtle could supposedly banish ghosts. In some Polynesian cultures, the turtle was even the symbol of the war god. The thing uniting all of these depictions is tenacity, endurance, and seeming invincibility paired with intelligence, bottomless wisdom, and a rather terrifying ability to be patient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 06-06-2016, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T09:16:54-07:00","id":908374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=908343#post908343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to Turtle, Calm and Contemplative, a good place to start would probably be Demantu the Abyssal Queen, a powerful Lune in War Against the Pure on pg. 127 It is worth noting that beyond being symbols of wisdom and longevity, turtle symbolism actually has a rather vicious dark side. In Nigeria the turtle is a trickster, the most cunning of all animals. In Ancient Egypt it was called &quot;an abomination to Ra&quot; and killed as an evil creature. It is associated with the Underworld in Ancient Egypt and in other cultures, and a leaf cut to resemble a turtle could supposedly banish ghosts. In some Polynesian cultures, the turtle was even the symbol of the war god. The thing uniting all of these depictions is tenacity, endurance, and seeming invincibility paired with intelligence, bottomless wisdom, and a rather terrifying ability to be patient.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, I was open to the idea that - in addition to travelling through the Astral and the Worlds of Spirit and Flesh - Turtle might also be found swimming through the Ocean Beyond Life. And with regards to Arcana, Death kept coming to mind as a choice. However, turtles have also been regarded as symbols of <i>creation</i> in a few other cultures, which could be reflected by ties to the Life Arcanum?<br /> <br /> That being said, I <i>am</i> thinking Turtle could be a Rank <i>7</i> Pangaean, with the ability to access and make use of more than just one of the Arcana. At least two at minimum, with four as the maximum. And if using the house rules for statting god-like entities (see Apep in my homebrew hub), then perhaps Numina slots could be sacrificed to give him extra Arcana?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-07-2016, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T23:14:53-07:00","id":909876,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it was mentioned before, but is it me or that Mountain is that thing which turns children into cannibals from Asylum? How would someone would present it as a Pangean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T03:26:47-07:00","id":917903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=909876#post909876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if it was mentioned before, but is it me or that Mountain is that thing which turns children into cannibals from Asylum? How would someone would present it as a Pangean?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea yet on how to represent it as a Pangaean, but could you name which pages in Asylum I should look up to read more on that 'thing'?<br /> <br /> Also, here's another stab at Turtle. As usual, I'm using the rules for Godlike Entities made by amechra and Arcanist. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Turtle, Calm and Contemplative</u></b><br /> <b>Type:</b> Pangaean<br /> <b>Rank:</b> 7<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Turtles 5, Water 2<br /> <b>Arcana:</b> Death 5, Spirit 5, Life 2, Matter 2<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Fate Sense, Omen Trance, Pathfinder, Essence Thief, Drain","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T04:39:42-07:00","id":917949,"title":"","content":"pages 114-119 (option 1 for Girl in the Snow). I imagine it would have dots in Mind, not only because it brainwash children to do its bidding, but also because of it themes- the Mountain is greater than you, bigger than you, older than you. It was before you and would stay after you. It knows every old secret which hides beneath its roots, every dark whisper which was buried in its caves. You are in awe when looking at it, you are not worthy to climb it. It blocks every other possibility, it is the boundary which can not be crossed. You wishes and dreams hide its top, your fears and secrets lurk at its bottom, it separates what is and isn't with its massive body. Be humble before the Mountain, and bow before its name- and maybe, just maybe, it would decide you are worthy enough to live.<br /> <br /> (think something like He Who Lives in Thrall from Exalted)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T05:02:21-07:00","id":917958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=917949#post917949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine it would have dots in Mind, not only because it brainwash children to do its bidding, but also because of it themes- the Mountain is greater than you, bigger than you, older than you. It was before you and would stay after you. It knows every old secret which hides beneath its roots, every dark whisper which was buried in its caves. You are in awe when looking at it, you are not worthy to climb it. It blocks every other possibility, it is the boundary which can not be crossed. You wishes and dreams hide its top, your fears and secrets lurk at its bottom, it separates what is and isn't with its massive body. Be humble before the Mountain, and bow before its name- and maybe, just maybe, it would decide you are worthy enough to live.<br /> <br /> (think something like He Who Lives in Thrall from Exalted)</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know who that is. But I can definitely see the Mountain having Mind 5. Maybe a bit of Space, too? Plus, I can imagine Mountain (while it was still alive) having been venerated by some Forest-Wise due to its nature being resonant with their Path.<br /> <br /> On a related note, what do you think of my current notes on Turtle?<br /> <br /> P.S: Found an interesting <a href=\"http://www.ilhawaii.net/~stony/1096myth.html\" target=\"_blank\">Native American story</a> that <i>might</i> help think up some history for Turtle in relation to his rapport (or perhaps lack of one) with Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-20-2016, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T06:47:47-07:00","id":917997,"title":"","content":"Note that everyone is really fucking scared of the ocean for good reason; I would generally veer towards Pangaeans associated with water and the beasts therein to be absolutely<i>\u200b terrifying.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T06:52:18-07:00","id":918001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=917958#post917958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P.S: Found an interesting <a href=\"http://www.ilhawaii.net/~stony/1096myth.html\" target=\"_blank\">Native American story</a> that <i>might</i> help think up some history for Turtle in relation to his rapport (or perhaps lack of one) with Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of stories, I can't help but recall the one about the <a href=\"http://changelog.ca/topic/The%20Scorpion%20and%20the%20Turtle\" target=\"_blank\">Turtle and the Scorpion</a>. And then remembering that Irem was associated with Scorpion imagery...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T08:14:06-07:00","id":918051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=917997#post917997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that everyone is really fucking scared of the ocean for good reason; I would generally veer towards Pangaeans associated with water and the beasts therein to be absolutely<i>\u200b terrifying.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of water-based Pangaeans, perhaps Tha'hon from Predators might have been one of them? I could certainly see that fitting with the Drowned God option, as the Deep could be a Pangaean that became a flesh-bound Horror in the centuries after the Sundering. Unlike most such beings, this one could still be alive in your setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=918001#post918001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of stories, I can't help but recall the one about the <a href=\"http://changelog.ca/topic/The%20Scorpion%20and%20the%20Turtle\" target=\"_blank\">Turtle and the Scorpion</a>. And then remembering that Irem was associated with Scorpion imagery...</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps that could spawn ideas for putting the Pangaean in an Arisen-related setting? Lol. Anyway, here's more stuff for me on Turtle. <hr /><br /> <b>Description:</b> One of the greater gods of the Border Marches, it is said that this Pangaean rivals <i>Urfarah </i>in age as well as power. Such a claim is backed by his ability to venture out of the Border Marches unchallenged in order to roam the Worlds of Spirit and Flesh.<br /> <br /> Turtle is honored by the People. His animals make their homes in the River, and priests and shamans invoke his name to honor or tame the river-spirits so that their villages thrive. However, he is also called to act as a guide for the dead, so that they may reach the Underworld and make their final descent into its dark waters. Hence, his role is a dualistic one in the pantheon of the gods. Creator and Destroyer. Life and Death.<br /> <br /> Many among the Wise and Uratha have tales on why Turtle is given a wide berth by even the Great Predator. Some say that the two Pangaeans clashed in a great battle not unlike the one between Wolf and Bull. Others suspect that Turtle found some secret of the Marches that gave him an edge against his fellow gods, including <i>Urfarah</i>. Whatever the reason, Turtle wanders freely as a result, and often travels to a world on either end of Pangaea in pursuit of his own agendas. Not only that, but the Wise have discovered the Pangaean also spending much time in the Astral Realm, and even the Ocean Beyond Life.<br /> <br /> In the World of Flesh, the People seldom find themselves graced by Turtle's presence. The Pangaean secludes himself in the oceans of whichever world he is in. And he seldom strays far from the shore in those few times he sets foot on land. This relative isolation may be another reason why Wolf refrains from hunting him.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Turtle is revered by other tribes besides the People. Islanders and seafarers feel the Pangaean's influence more strongly in the waters of their homes, and the Wise among their number often seek him out for knowledge and a number of other boons. These Awakened cultivate a relationship with Turtle and other waterborne gods of the Marches that is not always positive, but nowhere near as hostile as that of the land-based Vinca.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 06-20-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T15:00:28-07:00","id":918261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=917997#post917997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that everyone is really fucking scared of the ocean for good reason; I would generally veer towards Pangaeans associated with water and the beasts therein to be absolutely<i>\u200b terrifying.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Relevant as ever:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted doesn\u2019t make much of high-fidelity modern concept \u201cgods\u201d like spirits of gravity or oxygen because it is approaching the game from the position of a myth. If you take a look at mythological pantheons you won\u2019t find a major god of \u201cshit falls when you drop it\u201d because people were more concerned with things like \u201cthunder scares the shit out of me\u201d and \u201c<b>the ocean is a realm of nightmare and terrors beyond imagining.</b>\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T23:12:47-07:00","id":954851,"title":"","content":"So! Seeing as this hasn't had any new posts lately, I'd like to revive this thread with one question. Aside from being limited to Unfleshed and Extempores at least, would Neolithic Prometheans be limited to the five simple Refinements? Or would some/all of the complex ones also be present?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T00:29:10-07:00","id":954872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=954851#post954851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So! Seeing as this hasn't had any new posts lately, I'd like to revive this thread with one question. Aside from being limited to Unfleshed and Extempores at least, would Neolithic Prometheans be limited to the five simple Refinements? Or would some/all of the complex ones also be present?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that you need Complex Refinements to complete the Pilgrimage, you'd either discover them eventually, die, or wander the earth until someone else teaches them to you. While it makes sense to me that a qashmal would find you and teach you the Refinements you needed, that last option - playing a Created who dates back to the dawn of mankind, and has their Great Work span thousands of years - could be a stunning chronicle with a capable Storyteller. Considering that Bronze is beyond the scope of The Sundered World's timeline, the Refinement of Aes is likely outside of the first Created's hands unless they wander into Anatolia or Egypt and witness its creation. That said, Argentum seems an easy fit in a world with much more visible spirits, werewolves, and Wise.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I'd probably disallow the Unfleshed but accept both the Ulgan and Constructs of any element/humour using the rules for Extempore. Obsession can take root in any man and provide a conduit for the Divine Fire, so it stands to reason some childless woman in the village might attempt to create a child of clay and sticks using a ritual from a strange dream, or a grieving man might attempt to bring back his lover by offering their corpse up to the wilderness and the spirits within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T06:52:19-07:00","id":954927,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, why disallow Unfleshed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T10:46:07-07:00","id":958286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/868514-open-invite-the-sundered-world-chronicles?p=954927#post954927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, why disallow Unfleshed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Especially since it was implied in their writeup that they have existed for as long as people made effigies of themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T20:35:51-08:00","id":1054177,"title":"","content":"Idea related to the Pangaeans. Is it possible to tie the Pangaean worshipped by the Halaf to one of the Horrors found in Predators? Specifically, I wanted to make their mother goddess another possible identity for Aharnuz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}